1
00:00:47,714 --> 00:00:50,831
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

2
00:01:14,783 --> 00:01:17,115
[GASPING]

3
00:01:17,286 --> 00:01:18,901
Sméagol!

4
00:01:19,079 --> 00:01:20,410
I've got one!

5
00:01:20,581 --> 00:01:21,946
[LAUGHS]

6
00:01:22,124 --> 00:01:23,955
I've got a fish, Sméag. Sméagol!

7
00:01:24,126 --> 00:01:27,243
Pull it in. Go on. Go on. Go on.
Pull it in.

8
00:01:28,422 --> 00:01:29,878
[YELLS]

9
00:01:35,470 --> 00:01:37,301
SMÉAGOL:
Déagol!

10
00:02:01,121 --> 00:02:04,238
[GASPING AND COUGHING]

11
00:02:28,065 --> 00:02:31,182
[BIRDS SQUAWKING,
WINGS FLUTTERING]

12
00:02:34,696 --> 00:02:36,527
SMÉAGOL:
Déagol?

13
00:02:37,658 --> 00:02:38,989
[SMÉAGOL LAUGHS]

14
00:02:39,159 --> 00:02:41,320
Déagol.

15
00:02:57,135 --> 00:02:59,217
Give us that, Déagol, my love.

16
00:03:04,184 --> 00:03:05,469
Why?

17
00:03:06,561 --> 00:03:08,802
Because...

18
00:03:08,980 --> 00:03:12,723
...it's my birthday and I wants it.

19
00:03:23,286 --> 00:03:25,572
[GRUNTING]

20
00:03:29,501 --> 00:03:30,991
[SNARLING]

21
00:03:35,507 --> 00:03:37,372
[SCREAMS]

22
00:03:46,184 --> 00:03:48,675
[YELLING]

23
00:03:59,489 --> 00:04:01,980
[HEARTBEAT PULSING]

24
00:04:17,048 --> 00:04:20,165
[HEARTBEAT SLOWS, STOPS]

25
00:04:37,402 --> 00:04:41,736
[VOICE OF THE RING
SPEAKING IN BLACK SPEECH]

26
00:04:46,787 --> 00:04:52,032
My precious.

27
00:04:57,047 --> 00:04:59,413
[SHRIEKING]

28
00:04:59,591 --> 00:05:02,503
GOLLUM:
<i>They cursed us.</i>

29
00:05:02,677 --> 00:05:04,042
[WHISPERS]
<i>Murderer.</i>

30
00:05:04,221 --> 00:05:06,678
<i>"Murderer" they called us.</i>

31
00:05:06,848 --> 00:05:11,638
<i>They cursed us</i>
<i>and drove us away.</i>

32
00:05:12,771 --> 00:05:14,477
Gollum.

33
00:05:14,648 --> 00:05:16,354
Gollum.

34
00:05:16,525 --> 00:05:18,356
Gollum.

35
00:05:18,527 --> 00:05:19,983
[CROAKS]

36
00:05:20,278 --> 00:05:21,859
[SOBS]

37
00:05:22,030 --> 00:05:25,022
<i>And we wept, precious.</i>

38
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:28,784
<i>We wept to be so alone.</i>

39
00:05:28,995 --> 00:05:31,202
[GOLLUM SINGING]

40
00:05:31,373 --> 00:05:35,161
<i>--and cool</i>
<i>So nice for feet</i>

41
00:05:36,169 --> 00:05:40,538
<i>And we only wish</i>
<i>To catch a fish</i>

42
00:05:40,715 --> 00:05:43,957
<i>So juicy sweet</i>

43
00:05:49,724 --> 00:05:53,842
<i>And we forgot the taste of bread...</i>

44
00:05:54,020 --> 00:05:57,638
<i>...the sound of trees...</i>

45
00:05:58,525 --> 00:06:01,733
<i>...the softness of the wind.</i>

46
00:06:02,362 --> 00:06:08,028
<i>We even forgot our own name.</i>

47
00:06:16,167 --> 00:06:22,584
<i>My precious.</i>

48
00:07:02,172 --> 00:07:04,254
[RUSTLING]

49
00:07:04,799 --> 00:07:06,664
[GOLLUM PANTING]

50
00:07:06,843 --> 00:07:09,084
Wake up!

51
00:07:10,138 --> 00:07:11,799
Wake up!

52
00:07:11,973 --> 00:07:13,759
Wake up, sleepies.

53
00:07:13,934 --> 00:07:15,799
We must go, yes.

54
00:07:15,977 --> 00:07:18,639
We must go at once.

55
00:07:22,192 --> 00:07:25,275
Haven't you had any sleep, Mr. Frodo?

56
00:07:27,489 --> 00:07:30,026
I've gone and had too much.

57
00:07:31,409 --> 00:07:33,149
Must be getting late.

58
00:07:33,328 --> 00:07:34,818
FRODO:
No.

59
00:07:34,996 --> 00:07:36,907
It isn't.

60
00:07:37,082 --> 00:07:40,119
It isn't midday yet.

61
00:07:40,293 --> 00:07:42,375
The days are growing darker.

62
00:07:42,545 --> 00:07:44,786
[RUMBLING]

63
00:07:47,133 --> 00:07:49,340
Come on!

64
00:07:51,763 --> 00:07:54,004
Must go! No time!

65
00:07:54,182 --> 00:07:56,548
Not before Mr. Frodo's
had something to eat.

66
00:07:56,726 --> 00:07:59,593
GOLLUM:
No time to lose, silly.

67
00:08:08,363 --> 00:08:09,648
SAM:
Here.

68
00:08:12,867 --> 00:08:14,698
What about you?

69
00:08:14,869 --> 00:08:18,236
Oh, no, I'm not hungry.
Leastways, not for lembas bread.

70
00:08:18,832 --> 00:08:20,197
Sam.

71
00:08:22,794 --> 00:08:24,330
All right.

72
00:08:24,504 --> 00:08:26,995
We don't have that much left.

73
00:08:27,173 --> 00:08:30,040
We have to be careful
or we're going to run out.

74
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:35,132
You go ahead and eat that, Mr. Frodo.

75
00:08:35,306 --> 00:08:36,716
I've rationed it.

76
00:08:37,225 --> 00:08:38,886
There should be enough.

77
00:08:41,062 --> 00:08:42,268
For what?

78
00:08:43,940 --> 00:08:45,680
The journey home.

79
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:55,865
GOLLUM:
Come, Hobbitses.

80
00:08:57,245 --> 00:08:59,110
Very close now.

81
00:08:59,289 --> 00:09:02,531
Very close to Mordor.

82
00:09:02,709 --> 00:09:05,371
No safe places here.

83
00:09:05,545 --> 00:09:07,706
Hurry.

84
00:09:46,961 --> 00:09:49,873
[TREES GROANING]

85
00:09:55,970 --> 00:09:59,087
[MERRY AND PIPPIN LAUGHING]

86
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:01,806
MERRY:
It's good.

87
00:10:02,727 --> 00:10:04,467
Definitely from the Shire.

88
00:10:06,689 --> 00:10:08,805
Longbottom Leaf.

89
00:10:10,026 --> 00:10:11,891
[MOANS]

90
00:10:14,155 --> 00:10:18,489
I feel like I'm back at
The Green Dragon.

91
00:10:18,743 --> 00:10:22,827
-Mmm. Green Dragon.
-A mug of ale in my hand.

92
00:10:22,997 --> 00:10:27,582
Putting my feet up on a settle
after a hard day's work.

93
00:10:28,169 --> 00:10:31,627
Only, you've never done
a hard day's work.

94
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:33,171
[MURMURS INDISTINCTLY]

95
00:10:33,341 --> 00:10:35,172
[BOTH LAUGH]

96
00:10:44,435 --> 00:10:47,472
Welcome, my lords...

97
00:10:47,647 --> 00:10:49,888
...to Isengard!

98
00:10:50,275 --> 00:10:54,018
You young rascals!
A merry hunt you've led us on...

99
00:10:54,195 --> 00:10:59,189
...and now we find you feasting
and...and smoking!

100
00:10:59,367 --> 00:11:02,575
We are sitting on a field of victory...

101
00:11:02,745 --> 00:11:06,203
...enjoying a few well-earned comforts.

102
00:11:07,292 --> 00:11:11,126
The salted pork is particularly good.

103
00:11:11,671 --> 00:11:14,037
Salted pork?

104
00:11:14,757 --> 00:11:18,670
-Huh. Hobbits.
-We're under orders from Treebeard...

105
00:11:18,845 --> 00:11:21,678
...who's taken over management
of Isengard.

106
00:11:22,015 --> 00:11:24,051
[TREEBEARD GROANING]

107
00:11:24,225 --> 00:11:27,217
TREEBEARD:
Young Master Gandalf.

108
00:11:27,395 --> 00:11:31,980
I'm glad you've come.

109
00:11:32,150 --> 00:11:36,564
Wood and water, stock and stone
I can master.

110
00:11:36,738 --> 00:11:40,401
But there is a wizard to manage here...

111
00:11:40,575 --> 00:11:42,566
...locked in his tower.

112
00:11:45,246 --> 00:11:46,577
Show yourself.

113
00:11:46,831 --> 00:11:48,537
Be careful.

114
00:11:49,292 --> 00:11:51,954
Even in defeat, Saruman is dangerous.

115
00:11:52,128 --> 00:11:54,210
Well, let's just have his head
and be done with it.

116
00:11:54,380 --> 00:11:56,462
No.

117
00:11:56,799 --> 00:11:59,131
We need him alive.

118
00:12:00,136 --> 00:12:02,673
We need him to talk.

119
00:12:04,557 --> 00:12:08,800
SARUMAN: You have fought many wars
and slain many men, Théoden King...

120
00:12:08,978 --> 00:12:10,468
...and made peace afterwards.

121
00:12:10,647 --> 00:12:15,562
Can we not take counsel together
as we once did, my old friend?

122
00:12:15,777 --> 00:12:18,985
Can we not have peace, you and I?

123
00:12:19,155 --> 00:12:21,020
We shall have peace.

124
00:12:22,992 --> 00:12:25,074
We shall have peace...

125
00:12:25,286 --> 00:12:29,325
...when you answer
for the burning of the Westfold...

126
00:12:29,499 --> 00:12:32,206
...and the children that lie dead there!

127
00:12:33,002 --> 00:12:37,166
We shall have peace
when the lives of the soldiers...

128
00:12:37,340 --> 00:12:39,376
...whose bodies were hewn
even as they lay dead...

129
00:12:39,550 --> 00:12:43,088
...against the gates of the Hornburg,
are avenged!

130
00:12:44,681 --> 00:12:50,221
When you hang from a gibbet
for the sport of your own crows...

131
00:12:51,187 --> 00:12:53,394
...we shall have peace.

132
00:12:56,192 --> 00:12:58,854
Gibbets and crows?

133
00:12:59,195 --> 00:13:00,435
Dotard!

134
00:13:01,906 --> 00:13:04,739
What do you want, Gandalf Greyhame?

135
00:13:05,743 --> 00:13:08,234
Let me guess. The Key of Orthanc.

136
00:13:08,413 --> 00:13:11,371
Or perhaps the Keys of Barad-dûr itself...

137
00:13:11,541 --> 00:13:15,534
...along with the crowns of the seven kings
and the rods of the Five Wizards!

138
00:13:15,712 --> 00:13:18,624
Your treachery has already cost
many lives.

139
00:13:18,840 --> 00:13:21,206
Thousands more are now at risk.

140
00:13:21,384 --> 00:13:23,716
But you could save them, Saruman.

141
00:13:23,886 --> 00:13:26,218
You were deep in the enemy's counsel.

142
00:13:26,389 --> 00:13:29,631
So you have come here for information.

143
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:32,391
I have some for you.

144
00:13:37,859 --> 00:13:40,771
Something festers
in the heart of Middle-earth.

145
00:13:40,945 --> 00:13:43,231
Something that you have failed to see.

146
00:13:45,742 --> 00:13:49,234
But the Great Eye has seen it.

147
00:13:50,246 --> 00:13:53,955
Even now he presses his advantage.

148
00:13:55,752 --> 00:13:59,085
His attack will come soon.

149
00:14:01,257 --> 00:14:03,418
You're all going to die.

150
00:14:05,928 --> 00:14:09,136
But you know this, don't you, Gandalf?

151
00:14:09,307 --> 00:14:13,926
You cannot think that this Ranger
will ever sit upon the throne of Gondor.

152
00:14:14,103 --> 00:14:20,190
This exile, crept from the shadows,
will never be crowned king.

153
00:14:21,527 --> 00:14:25,190
Gandalf does not hesitate
to sacrifice those closest to him...

154
00:14:26,115 --> 00:14:28,322
...those he professes to love.

155
00:14:29,410 --> 00:14:33,949
Tell me, what words of comfort
did you give the Halfling...

156
00:14:34,123 --> 00:14:36,489
...before you sent him to his doom?

157
00:14:36,667 --> 00:14:38,578
[SIGHS]

158
00:14:39,545 --> 00:14:44,289
The path that you have set him on
can only lead to death.

159
00:14:44,634 --> 00:14:46,795
I've heard enough!

160
00:14:46,969 --> 00:14:48,800
Shoot him.
Stick an arrow in his gob.

161
00:14:49,305 --> 00:14:50,966
GANDALF:
No.

162
00:14:51,432 --> 00:14:53,639
Come down, Saruman...

163
00:14:53,810 --> 00:14:57,723
-...and your life will be spared.
-Save your pity and your mercy.

164
00:14:57,939 --> 00:14:59,224
I have no use for it!

165
00:15:08,533 --> 00:15:09,989
GANDALF:
Saruman...

166
00:15:11,035 --> 00:15:12,991
...your staff is broken.

167
00:15:13,162 --> 00:15:15,027
[GASPS]

168
00:15:25,007 --> 00:15:28,499
Gríma, you need not follow him.

169
00:15:29,679 --> 00:15:32,341
You were not always as you are now.

170
00:15:32,515 --> 00:15:35,348
You were once a Man of Rohan.

171
00:15:35,518 --> 00:15:36,724
Come down.

172
00:15:36,894 --> 00:15:39,601
A Man of Rohan?

173
00:15:40,523 --> 00:15:42,764
What is the house of Rohan...

174
00:15:42,984 --> 00:15:46,602
...but a thatched barn
where brigands drink in the reek...

175
00:15:46,779 --> 00:15:50,522
...and their brats roll on the floor
with the dogs?

176
00:15:51,033 --> 00:15:57,495
The victory at Helm's Deep does not
belong to you, Théoden Horse-master.

177
00:15:58,082 --> 00:16:02,701
You are a lesser son of greater sires.

178
00:16:05,047 --> 00:16:06,708
Gríma...

179
00:16:07,550 --> 00:16:09,415
...come down.

180
00:16:09,760 --> 00:16:11,216
Be free of him.

181
00:16:11,387 --> 00:16:15,380
-Free? He will never be free.
-No.

182
00:16:15,725 --> 00:16:18,387
Get down, cur!

183
00:16:18,561 --> 00:16:19,892
[GRUNTS]

184
00:16:20,062 --> 00:16:21,393
Saruman!

185
00:16:21,564 --> 00:16:24,226
You were deep in the enemy's counsel.

186
00:16:24,734 --> 00:16:26,895
Tell us what you know!

187
00:16:28,404 --> 00:16:33,615
You withdraw your guard, and I will tell you
where your doom will be decided.

188
00:16:33,784 --> 00:16:36,742
I will not be held prisoner here.

189
00:16:36,913 --> 00:16:38,449
[GASPS]

190
00:16:41,792 --> 00:16:43,328
[GRUNTS]

191
00:16:43,503 --> 00:16:45,789
[PANTING]

192
00:17:04,524 --> 00:17:06,060
Send word to all our allies...

193
00:17:06,234 --> 00:17:09,101
...and to every corner of Middle-earth
that still stands free.

194
00:17:09,612 --> 00:17:12,775
The enemy moves against us.
We need to know where he will strike.

195
00:17:12,949 --> 00:17:14,985
[CREAKING]

196
00:17:31,968 --> 00:17:35,881
The filth of Saruman...

197
00:17:36,097 --> 00:17:39,885
...is washing away.

198
00:17:40,101 --> 00:17:44,640
Trees will come back to live here.

199
00:17:45,147 --> 00:17:47,308
Young trees.

200
00:17:47,483 --> 00:17:49,644
-Wild trees.
-Pippin!

201
00:17:59,161 --> 00:18:01,322
Bless my bark!

202
00:18:01,497 --> 00:18:03,328
GANDALF:
Peregrin Took!

203
00:18:03,499 --> 00:18:06,161
I'll take that, my lad.

204
00:18:06,335 --> 00:18:08,166
Quickly, now.

205
00:18:58,387 --> 00:19:03,927
THÉODEN: Tonight we remember those
who gave their blood to defend this country.

206
00:19:04,602 --> 00:19:06,638
Hail the victorious dead.

207
00:19:06,812 --> 00:19:08,222
ALL:
Hail!

208
00:19:14,236 --> 00:19:17,319
[CHATTERING AND LAUGHING]

209
00:19:19,241 --> 00:19:21,106
No pauses.

210
00:19:21,285 --> 00:19:25,449
-No spills.
-And no regurgitation.

211
00:19:25,956 --> 00:19:27,617
So it's a drinking game?

212
00:19:27,792 --> 00:19:29,123
[CHEERING]

213
00:19:29,293 --> 00:19:31,784
Last one standing wins.

214
00:19:36,133 --> 00:19:38,294
MAN:
What'll we drink to? Let's drink to victory!

215
00:19:38,469 --> 00:19:39,800
MEN:
To victory!

216
00:19:40,096 --> 00:19:42,303
[GULPING]

217
00:19:52,525 --> 00:19:54,811
[SPEAKING IN ELVISH]

218
00:20:23,806 --> 00:20:25,467
THÉODEN:
I am happy for you.

219
00:20:25,808 --> 00:20:28,265
He is an honorable man.

220
00:20:28,644 --> 00:20:31,135
You are both honorable men.

221
00:20:32,982 --> 00:20:38,318
It was not Théoden of Rohan
who led our people to victory.

222
00:20:45,202 --> 00:20:48,319
Ah, don't listen to me.

223
00:20:49,165 --> 00:20:50,655
You are young.

224
00:20:50,833 --> 00:20:53,165
And tonight is for you.

225
00:21:03,220 --> 00:21:05,085
[FARTS]

226
00:21:05,890 --> 00:21:07,346
[LAUGHS]

227
00:21:07,516 --> 00:21:09,177
Here, here.

228
00:21:10,686 --> 00:21:16,556
It's the Dwarves that go swimming
with little, hairy women.

229
00:21:17,735 --> 00:21:19,521
[BELCHES]

230
00:21:21,947 --> 00:21:23,187
I feel something.

231
00:21:25,367 --> 00:21:27,858
A slight tingle in my fingers.

232
00:21:28,537 --> 00:21:30,118
I think it's affecting me.

233
00:21:30,539 --> 00:21:31,870
[LAUGHS]

234
00:21:32,041 --> 00:21:33,747
What did I say?

235
00:21:33,918 --> 00:21:37,251
[SLURRING]
He can't hold his liquor.

236
00:21:44,595 --> 00:21:45,926
Game over.

237
00:21:46,096 --> 00:21:48,462
MERRY & PIPPIN [SINGING]:
<i>Oh, you can search far and wide</i>

238
00:21:48,641 --> 00:21:50,097
<i>You can drink the whole town dry</i>

239
00:21:50,267 --> 00:21:53,634
<i>But you'll never find a beer so brown</i>
<i>But you'll never find a beer so brown</i>

240
00:21:53,854 --> 00:21:58,223
<i>As the one we drink in our hometown</i>
<i>As the one we drink in our hometown</i>

241
00:21:58,400 --> 00:22:02,268
<i>You can drink your fancy ales</i>
<i>You can drink 'em by the flagon</i>

242
00:22:02,446 --> 00:22:05,609
<i>But the only brew for the brave and true</i>

243
00:22:08,244 --> 00:22:09,575
Pippin!

244
00:22:09,995 --> 00:22:13,078
MERRY & PIPPIN [SINGING]:
<i>But the only brew for the brave and true</i>

245
00:22:13,415 --> 00:22:15,451
<i>Comes from The Green Dragon</i>

246
00:22:15,626 --> 00:22:17,912
[CROWD CHEERING]

247
00:22:18,796 --> 00:22:21,629
MERRY:
Thank you! I win!

248
00:22:23,425 --> 00:22:25,916
No news of Frodo?

249
00:22:26,095 --> 00:22:29,587
No word. Nothing.

250
00:22:30,432 --> 00:22:32,593
We have time.

251
00:22:34,103 --> 00:22:37,391
Every day, Frodo moves closer to Mordor.

252
00:22:38,107 --> 00:22:40,189
Do we know that?

253
00:22:44,029 --> 00:22:45,769
What does your heart tell you?

254
00:22:52,788 --> 00:22:56,121
That Frodo is alive.

255
00:22:58,294 --> 00:23:00,125
Yes.

256
00:23:02,673 --> 00:23:04,664
Yes, he's alive.

257
00:23:07,136 --> 00:23:09,969
GOLLUM:
Too risky. Too risky.

258
00:23:10,139 --> 00:23:11,345
Thieves.

259
00:23:11,515 --> 00:23:13,551
They stole it from us.

260
00:23:13,726 --> 00:23:16,809
Kill them. Kill them. Kill them both.

261
00:23:16,979 --> 00:23:18,389
[YELLS]

262
00:23:18,564 --> 00:23:22,148
Shh! Quiet! Mustn't wake them.

263
00:23:22,318 --> 00:23:24,809
Mustn't ruin it now.

264
00:23:24,987 --> 00:23:27,069
But they knows.

265
00:23:27,239 --> 00:23:29,150
They knows.

266
00:23:29,325 --> 00:23:31,941
They suspects us.

267
00:23:33,162 --> 00:23:36,654
What's it saying, my precious, my love?

268
00:23:36,832 --> 00:23:40,450
Is Sméagol losing his nerve?

269
00:23:41,086 --> 00:23:43,498
No. Not.

270
00:23:43,672 --> 00:23:47,881
Never. Sméagol hates nasty Hobbitses.

271
00:23:48,052 --> 00:23:52,887
Sméagol wants to see them dead.

272
00:23:53,057 --> 00:23:55,594
And we will.

273
00:23:55,768 --> 00:23:59,852
Sméagol did it once.
He can do it again.

274
00:24:03,192 --> 00:24:05,854
It's ours!

275
00:24:06,028 --> 00:24:08,690
Ours!

276
00:24:09,782 --> 00:24:12,694
We must get the precious.
We must get it back.

277
00:24:12,868 --> 00:24:16,235
Patience! Patience, my love.

278
00:24:16,413 --> 00:24:20,782
First we must lead them to her.

279
00:24:21,710 --> 00:24:26,704
We lead them to the Winding Stair.

280
00:24:26,882 --> 00:24:29,544
Yes, the stairs. And then?

281
00:24:29,718 --> 00:24:32,710
Up, up, up, up,
up the stairs we go...

282
00:24:32,888 --> 00:24:39,259
...until we come to the tunnel.

283
00:24:39,645 --> 00:24:42,762
And when they go in...

284
00:24:42,940 --> 00:24:45,727
...there's no coming out.

285
00:24:46,652 --> 00:24:49,564
She's always hungry.

286
00:24:50,280 --> 00:24:54,489
She always needs to feed.

287
00:24:54,660 --> 00:24:56,070
She must eat.

288
00:24:56,245 --> 00:24:58,406
All she gets is filthy Orcses.

289
00:24:58,580 --> 00:25:01,287
And they doesn't taste very nice,
does they, precious?

290
00:25:01,917 --> 00:25:03,578
No.

291
00:25:03,752 --> 00:25:08,416
Not very nice at all, my love.

292
00:25:08,590 --> 00:25:11,423
She hungers for sweeter meats.

293
00:25:11,593 --> 00:25:13,424
Hobbit meat.

294
00:25:13,595 --> 00:25:18,430
And when she throws away the bones
and the empty clothes...

295
00:25:18,600 --> 00:25:21,637
...then we will find it.

296
00:25:21,812 --> 00:25:26,146
And take it for me!

297
00:25:27,943 --> 00:25:29,308
For us.

298
00:25:29,820 --> 00:25:32,812
Yes. We meant "for us."

299
00:25:32,990 --> 00:25:36,448
Gollum. Gollum.

300
00:25:36,618 --> 00:25:41,112
The precious will be ours...

301
00:25:41,290 --> 00:25:45,784
...once the Hobbitses are dead!

302
00:25:46,295 --> 00:25:47,785
You treacherous little toad!

303
00:25:48,464 --> 00:25:50,295
[GOLLUM YELLING]

304
00:25:50,466 --> 00:25:52,798
No! No! Master!

305
00:25:52,968 --> 00:25:54,583
No, Sam! Leave him alone!

306
00:25:55,471 --> 00:25:58,133
I heard it from his own mouth.
He means to murder us.

307
00:25:58,307 --> 00:26:02,471
Never! Sméagol wouldn't hurt a fly.

308
00:26:02,978 --> 00:26:04,309
[YELLS]

309
00:26:04,480 --> 00:26:06,516
He's a horrid, fat Hobbit...

310
00:26:06,690 --> 00:26:08,305
...who hates Sméagol...

311
00:26:08,484 --> 00:26:11,226
...and who makes up nasty lies.

312
00:26:11,403 --> 00:26:14,110
You miserable little maggot!
I'll stove your head in!

313
00:26:14,490 --> 00:26:15,730
Sam!

314
00:26:16,158 --> 00:26:17,694
SAM:
Call me a liar? You're a liar!

315
00:26:17,868 --> 00:26:19,199
[YELLS]

316
00:26:19,369 --> 00:26:23,328
-You scare him off, we're lost!
-I don't care! I can't do it, Mr. Frodo.

317
00:26:23,499 --> 00:26:26,662
-I won't wait around for him to kill us!
-I'm not sending him away.

318
00:26:27,002 --> 00:26:28,333
SAM:
You don't see it, do you?

319
00:26:28,712 --> 00:26:30,168
He's a villain.

320
00:26:31,173 --> 00:26:34,757
We can't do this by ourselves, Sam.
Not without a guide.

321
00:26:35,636 --> 00:26:38,503
I need you on my side.

322
00:26:39,264 --> 00:26:41,630
I'm on your side, Mr. Frodo.

323
00:26:43,143 --> 00:26:46,055
I know, Sam. I know.

324
00:26:46,647 --> 00:26:48,603
Trust me.

325
00:26:48,774 --> 00:26:51,186
Come, Sméagol.

326
00:27:04,039 --> 00:27:06,405
[SNORING]

327
00:27:59,094 --> 00:28:00,584
What time is it?

328
00:28:02,931 --> 00:28:04,421
Not yet dawn.

329
00:28:11,315 --> 00:28:14,352
I dreamed I saw a great wave...

330
00:28:14,526 --> 00:28:18,519
...climbing over green lands
and above the hills.

331
00:28:19,781 --> 00:28:22,272
I stood upon the brink.

332
00:28:23,160 --> 00:28:26,323
It was utterly dark in the abyss
before my feet.

333
00:28:28,290 --> 00:28:31,032
A light shone behind me...

334
00:28:31,668 --> 00:28:34,125
...but I could not turn.

335
00:28:34,296 --> 00:28:37,663
I could only stand there, waiting.

336
00:28:39,134 --> 00:28:41,841
Night changes many thoughts.

337
00:28:42,262 --> 00:28:44,378
Sleep, Éowyn.

338
00:28:44,973 --> 00:28:47,180
Sleep...

339
00:28:49,895 --> 00:28:51,806
...while you can.

340
00:29:15,921 --> 00:29:18,207
The stars are veiled.

341
00:29:19,216 --> 00:29:22,708
Something stirs in the east.

342
00:29:23,387 --> 00:29:26,504
A sleepless malice.

343
00:29:28,600 --> 00:29:31,387
The Eye of the enemy is moving.

344
00:29:44,825 --> 00:29:47,532
MERRY:
What are you doing?

345
00:29:49,913 --> 00:29:51,995
[SNORING LIGHTLY]

346
00:29:52,165 --> 00:29:53,621
MERRY [WHISPERING]:
Pippin!

347
00:30:01,133 --> 00:30:02,873
Pippin?

348
00:30:07,389 --> 00:30:09,050
[MUTTERS INDISTINCTLY]

349
00:30:15,731 --> 00:30:17,062
Pippin.

350
00:30:17,733 --> 00:30:20,395
-What, are you mad?
-I just want to look at it.

351
00:30:20,569 --> 00:30:21,649
Just one more time.

352
00:30:21,903 --> 00:30:23,985
MERRY:
Put it back.

353
00:30:34,249 --> 00:30:36,080
Pippin.

354
00:30:39,755 --> 00:30:41,962
[GROWLING]

355
00:30:42,591 --> 00:30:44,081
No!

356
00:30:44,301 --> 00:30:46,166
[RUMBLING]

357
00:30:47,596 --> 00:30:49,052
[WHIMPERING]

358
00:30:49,222 --> 00:30:50,507
[IN NORMAL VOICE]
Pippin.

359
00:30:51,308 --> 00:30:53,640
[EERIE BREATHING]

360
00:30:53,810 --> 00:30:55,016
He is here.

361
00:30:55,187 --> 00:30:57,473
SAURON:
<i>I see you.</i>

362
00:31:00,484 --> 00:31:02,099
Pippin!

363
00:31:06,239 --> 00:31:08,321
[SAURON SPEAKING
IN BLACK SPEECH]

364
00:31:08,492 --> 00:31:10,778
[GRUNTING AND GASPING]

365
00:31:16,750 --> 00:31:19,492
MERRY:
Help! Gandalf, help!

366
00:31:21,254 --> 00:31:23,119
Someone help him!

367
00:31:29,513 --> 00:31:30,719
Pippin!

368
00:31:31,848 --> 00:31:33,088
Fool of a Took!

369
00:31:45,570 --> 00:31:47,652
[WHISPERS INDISTINCTLY]

370
00:31:51,660 --> 00:31:53,946
[GASPING]

371
00:31:54,204 --> 00:31:56,411
Look at me.

372
00:31:58,375 --> 00:32:02,493
Gandalf, forgive me.

373
00:32:02,671 --> 00:32:04,536
GANDALF:
Look at me.

374
00:32:04,714 --> 00:32:06,545
What did you see?

375
00:32:10,053 --> 00:32:12,135
A tree.

376
00:32:13,098 --> 00:32:14,963
There was a white tree...

377
00:32:15,142 --> 00:32:16,632
...in a courtyard of stone.

378
00:32:19,438 --> 00:32:20,723
It was dead.

379
00:32:24,901 --> 00:32:26,732
The city was burning.

380
00:32:26,903 --> 00:32:30,270
Minas Tirith? Is that what you saw?

381
00:32:30,949 --> 00:32:32,985
I saw....

382
00:32:36,371 --> 00:32:37,736
I saw him.

383
00:32:40,750 --> 00:32:42,991
I could hear his voice in my head.

384
00:32:43,170 --> 00:32:45,582
And what did you tell him?

385
00:32:45,755 --> 00:32:47,586
Speak!

386
00:32:51,761 --> 00:32:54,924
He asked me my name.
I didn't answer.

387
00:32:55,098 --> 00:32:56,554
He hurt me.

388
00:32:56,725 --> 00:32:59,182
What did you tell him
about Frodo and the Ring?

389
00:33:02,689 --> 00:33:05,146
There was no lie in Pippin's eyes.

390
00:33:05,984 --> 00:33:08,225
A fool...

391
00:33:08,403 --> 00:33:10,689
...but an honest fool he remains.

392
00:33:11,156 --> 00:33:14,694
He told Sauron nothing
of Frodo and the Ring.

393
00:33:15,744 --> 00:33:18,110
We've been strangely fortunate.

394
00:33:18,288 --> 00:33:22,156
Pippin saw in the palantír
a glimpse of the enemy's plan.

395
00:33:23,084 --> 00:33:27,043
Sauron moves to strike
the city of Minas Tirith.

396
00:33:27,631 --> 00:33:31,374
His defeat at Helm's Deep
showed our enemy one thing.

397
00:33:31,551 --> 00:33:33,883
He knows the heir of Elendil
has come forth.

398
00:33:34,054 --> 00:33:36,170
Men are not as weak as he supposed.

399
00:33:36,348 --> 00:33:40,136
There is courage still, strength
enough perhaps to challenge him.

400
00:33:40,352 --> 00:33:42,217
Sauron fears this.

401
00:33:42,395 --> 00:33:46,729
He will not risk the peoples of
Middle-earth uniting under one banner.

402
00:33:47,901 --> 00:33:50,313
He will raze Minas Tirith
to the ground...

403
00:33:50,487 --> 00:33:53,979
...before he sees a king
return to the throne of Men.

404
00:33:54,157 --> 00:33:58,070
If the beacons of Gondor are lit,
Rohan must be ready for war.

405
00:33:58,995 --> 00:34:01,202
Tell me...

406
00:34:01,373 --> 00:34:05,161
...why should we ride to the aid
of those who did not come to ours?

407
00:34:09,047 --> 00:34:10,878
What do we owe Gondor?

408
00:34:12,008 --> 00:34:14,044
-I will go.
-No!

409
00:34:14,219 --> 00:34:17,382
-They must be warned.
-They will be.

410
00:34:20,809 --> 00:34:23,346
You must come to Minas Tirith
by another road.

411
00:34:23,895 --> 00:34:28,355
Follow the river.
Look to the black ships.

412
00:34:29,317 --> 00:34:31,273
Understand this:

413
00:34:31,444 --> 00:34:35,107
Things are now in motion
that cannot be undone.

414
00:34:36,616 --> 00:34:38,698
I ride for Minas Tirith...

415
00:34:40,954 --> 00:34:43,616
...and I won't be going alone.

416
00:34:45,375 --> 00:34:49,038
Of all the inquisitive Hobbits,
Peregrin Took, you are the worst.

417
00:34:50,046 --> 00:34:51,707
Hurry! Hurry!

418
00:34:53,216 --> 00:34:54,626
Where are we going?

419
00:34:54,801 --> 00:34:56,041
Why did you look?

420
00:34:56,219 --> 00:34:58,961
Why do you always have to look?

421
00:34:59,139 --> 00:35:02,222
-I don't know. I can't help it.
-You never can.

422
00:35:02,684 --> 00:35:04,094
I'm sorry, all right?

423
00:35:06,187 --> 00:35:09,099
-I won't do it again.
-Don't you understand?

424
00:35:09,858 --> 00:35:11,814
The enemy thinks you have the Ring.

425
00:35:11,985 --> 00:35:15,728
He's going to be looking for you, Pip.
They have to get you out of here.

426
00:35:17,157 --> 00:35:19,819
And you--? You're coming with me?

427
00:35:22,037 --> 00:35:23,447
Merry?

428
00:35:23,622 --> 00:35:24,907
Come on.

429
00:35:30,420 --> 00:35:31,785
How far is Minas Tirith?

430
00:35:31,963 --> 00:35:34,579
Three days' ride, as the Nazgûl flies.

431
00:35:34,758 --> 00:35:38,250
And you better hope we don't have
one of those on our tail.

432
00:35:38,970 --> 00:35:40,460
Here.

433
00:35:40,639 --> 00:35:42,425
Something for the road.

434
00:35:43,308 --> 00:35:45,264
The last of the Longbottom Leaf.

435
00:35:45,435 --> 00:35:49,428
I know you've run out.
You smoke too much, Pippin.

436
00:35:49,606 --> 00:35:52,097
But-- But we'll see each other soon.

437
00:35:55,445 --> 00:35:57,936
-Won't we?
-I don't know.

438
00:35:59,824 --> 00:36:01,985
[TEARFULLY]
I don't know what's going to happen.

439
00:36:02,160 --> 00:36:03,866
-Merry.
-Run, Shadowfax.

440
00:36:04,037 --> 00:36:05,493
Show us the meaning of haste.

441
00:36:05,664 --> 00:36:07,575
Merry!

442
00:36:18,051 --> 00:36:19,166
Merry!

443
00:36:29,646 --> 00:36:31,136
He's always followed me...

444
00:36:31,815 --> 00:36:33,851
...everywhere I went...

445
00:36:34,192 --> 00:36:35,978
...since before we were tweens.

446
00:36:37,153 --> 00:36:41,066
I would get him into
the worst sort of trouble...

447
00:36:41,241 --> 00:36:43,323
...but I was always there to get him out.

448
00:36:45,787 --> 00:36:47,652
Now he's gone.

449
00:36:49,332 --> 00:36:52,244
Just like Frodo and Sam.

450
00:36:52,877 --> 00:36:55,619
One thing I have learned about Hobbits:

451
00:36:55,797 --> 00:36:57,458
They're a most hardy folk.

452
00:36:58,007 --> 00:37:01,716
Foolhardy, maybe. He's a Took.

453
00:37:16,192 --> 00:37:18,478
ELROND:
<i>Take her by the safest road.</i>

454
00:37:18,653 --> 00:37:21,144
<i>A ship lies anchored</i>
<i>in the Grey Havens.</i>

455
00:37:21,322 --> 00:37:25,190
<i>It waits to carry her across the sea.</i>

456
00:37:25,368 --> 00:37:28,735
<i>The last journey of Arwen Undómiel.</i>

457
00:37:34,335 --> 00:37:36,200
[WIND WHISTLING]

458
00:38:34,354 --> 00:38:37,437
There is nothing for you here...

459
00:38:37,941 --> 00:38:40,148
...only death.

460
00:38:47,450 --> 00:38:48,735
ELF ESCORT:
Lady Arwen...

461
00:38:49,661 --> 00:38:51,572
...we cannot delay.

462
00:38:54,040 --> 00:38:55,280
My lady!

463
00:39:14,686 --> 00:39:17,302
ARWEN: Tell me what you have seen.
ELROND: Arwen.

464
00:39:17,480 --> 00:39:19,436
ARWEN:
You have the gift of foresight.

465
00:39:19,607 --> 00:39:21,393
What did you see?

466
00:39:22,026 --> 00:39:25,359
I looked into your future,
and I saw death.

467
00:39:25,905 --> 00:39:28,021
But there is also life.

468
00:39:29,951 --> 00:39:33,990
You saw there was a child.
You saw my son.

469
00:39:34,622 --> 00:39:37,159
ELROND:
That future is almost gone.

470
00:39:37,333 --> 00:39:39,324
But it is not lost.

471
00:39:41,921 --> 00:39:44,128
Nothing is certain.

472
00:39:45,842 --> 00:39:48,549
Some things are certain.

473
00:39:52,348 --> 00:39:55,181
If I leave him now...

474
00:39:55,351 --> 00:39:57,967
...I will regret it forever.

475
00:39:59,063 --> 00:40:01,395
It is time.

476
00:40:06,654 --> 00:40:10,442
ARWEN:
<i>From the ashes a fire shall be woken</i>

477
00:40:10,617 --> 00:40:14,030
<i>A light from the shadow shall spring</i>

478
00:40:14,203 --> 00:40:17,491
<i>Renewed shall be blade that was broken</i>

479
00:40:20,293 --> 00:40:21,954
[SCREAMS]

480
00:40:24,881 --> 00:40:28,089
<i>The crownless again shall be king</i>

481
00:40:31,846 --> 00:40:33,882
Re-forge the sword.

482
00:40:35,516 --> 00:40:36,972
[SPEAKS IN ELVISH]

483
00:41:08,758 --> 00:41:11,465
ELROND:
Your hands are cold.

484
00:41:14,847 --> 00:41:17,964
The life of the Eldar is leaving you.

485
00:41:21,396 --> 00:41:23,307
This was my choice.

486
00:41:23,481 --> 00:41:24,971
[SPEAKS IN ELVISH]

487
00:41:25,149 --> 00:41:27,435
Whether by your will or not...

488
00:41:28,778 --> 00:41:33,067
...there is no ship now
that can bear me hence.

489
00:42:20,288 --> 00:42:23,121
We've just passed
into the realm of Gondor.

490
00:42:34,761 --> 00:42:37,002
Minas Tirith.

491
00:42:37,597 --> 00:42:39,929
City of kings.

492
00:43:11,297 --> 00:43:13,083
Make way!

493
00:43:42,286 --> 00:43:44,117
It's the tree.

494
00:43:44,288 --> 00:43:45,949
Gandalf. Gandalf.

495
00:43:46,124 --> 00:43:48,365
GANDALF:
Yes, the White Tree of Gondor.

496
00:43:48,543 --> 00:43:50,374
The tree of the king.

497
00:43:50,545 --> 00:43:53,207
Lord Denethor, however,
is not king.

498
00:43:53,381 --> 00:43:56,043
He is a steward only,
a caretaker of the throne.

499
00:43:56,801 --> 00:44:00,339
Now listen carefully.
Lord Denethor is Boromir's father.

500
00:44:00,888 --> 00:44:04,676
To give him news of his beloved son's
death would be most unwise.

501
00:44:05,143 --> 00:44:08,601
And do not mention Frodo or the Ring.

502
00:44:09,480 --> 00:44:12,222
And say nothing of Aragorn either.

503
00:44:14,068 --> 00:44:17,936
In fact, it's better if you
don't speak at all, Peregrin Took.

504
00:44:48,102 --> 00:44:54,598
Hail Denethor, son of Ecthelion,
lord and steward of Gondor.

505
00:45:00,114 --> 00:45:04,824
I come with tidings in this dark hour,
and with counsel.

506
00:45:05,786 --> 00:45:09,153
Perhaps you come to explain this.

507
00:45:14,795 --> 00:45:19,334
Perhaps you come to tell me
why my son is dead.

508
00:45:23,554 --> 00:45:25,886
[ARROWS WHISTLING]

509
00:45:26,057 --> 00:45:27,718
[SCREAMS]

510
00:45:31,896 --> 00:45:33,636
[ARROW IMPACTS]
[GRUNTS]

511
00:45:33,814 --> 00:45:36,806
Boromir died to save us...

512
00:45:36,984 --> 00:45:38,645
...my kinsman and me.

513
00:45:38,819 --> 00:45:42,311
-He fell defending us from many foes.
-Pippin.

514
00:45:47,828 --> 00:45:51,286
I offer you my service, such as it is...

515
00:45:51,832 --> 00:45:53,823
...in payment of this debt.

516
00:45:56,003 --> 00:45:59,336
This is my first command to you.

517
00:46:00,049 --> 00:46:03,507
How did you escape
and my son did not...

518
00:46:03,844 --> 00:46:06,176
...so mighty a man as he was?

519
00:46:06,847 --> 00:46:10,180
The mightiest man
may be slain by one arrow...

520
00:46:10,434 --> 00:46:12,345
...and Boromir was pierced by many.

521
00:46:16,482 --> 00:46:18,188
Get up.

522
00:46:18,359 --> 00:46:22,978
My lord, there will be a time
to grieve for Boromir...

523
00:46:23,447 --> 00:46:25,187
...but it is not now.

524
00:46:25,908 --> 00:46:28,115
War is coming.

525
00:46:28,452 --> 00:46:32,866
The enemy is on your doorstep.
As steward, you are charged...

526
00:46:33,040 --> 00:46:37,204
...with the defense of this city.
Where are Gondor's armies?

527
00:46:37,378 --> 00:46:42,247
You still have friends.
You are not alone in this fight.

528
00:46:42,425 --> 00:46:46,919
Send word to Théoden of Rohan.
Light the beacons.

529
00:46:48,514 --> 00:46:52,052
You think you are wise, Mithrandir.

530
00:46:52,226 --> 00:46:55,263
Yet for all your subtleties,
you have not wisdom.

531
00:46:57,398 --> 00:47:01,562
Do you think the eyes
of the White Tower are blind?

532
00:47:01,736 --> 00:47:04,819
I have seen more than you know.

533
00:47:04,989 --> 00:47:08,197
With your left hand you would use me
as a shield against Mordor.

534
00:47:08,367 --> 00:47:11,234
And with your right
you'd seek to supplant me.

535
00:47:11,412 --> 00:47:15,121
I know who rides with Théoden of Rohan.

536
00:47:15,291 --> 00:47:21,252
Oh, yes. Word has reached my ears
of this Aragorn, son of Arathorn.

537
00:47:21,422 --> 00:47:26,257
And I tell you now, I will not bow
to this Ranger from the North...

538
00:47:26,427 --> 00:47:30,921
...last of a ragged house
long bereft of lordship.

539
00:47:31,098 --> 00:47:36,934
Authority is not given to you
to deny the return of the king, steward.

540
00:47:37,104 --> 00:47:41,518
The rule of Gondor is mine
and no other's.

541
00:47:46,697 --> 00:47:48,483
GANDALF:
Come.

542
00:47:56,415 --> 00:47:58,997
All has turned to vain ambition.

543
00:47:59,168 --> 00:48:02,626
He would even use his grief
as a cloak.

544
00:48:05,508 --> 00:48:08,295
A thousand years
this city has stood.

545
00:48:09,387 --> 00:48:11,799
Now, at the whim of a madman,
it will fall.

546
00:48:13,015 --> 00:48:15,222
And the White Tree,
the tree of the king...

547
00:48:15,393 --> 00:48:16,929
...will never bloom again.

548
00:48:17,103 --> 00:48:18,809
PIPPIN:
Why are they still guarding it?

549
00:48:18,979 --> 00:48:21,015
GANDALF:
They guard it because they have hope.

550
00:48:21,190 --> 00:48:23,806
A faint and fading hope
that one day it will flower.

551
00:48:23,984 --> 00:48:28,728
That a king will come
and this city will be as it once was...

552
00:48:28,906 --> 00:48:31,818
...before it fell into decay.

553
00:48:31,992 --> 00:48:35,234
The old wisdom borne out
of the West was forsaken.

554
00:48:35,413 --> 00:48:39,702
Kings made tombs more splendid
than the houses of the living...

555
00:48:39,917 --> 00:48:41,828
...and counted the old names
of their descent...

556
00:48:42,002 --> 00:48:44,789
...dearer than the names of their sons.

557
00:48:44,964 --> 00:48:50,004
Childless lords sat in aged halls,
musing on heraldry...

558
00:48:50,177 --> 00:48:55,513
...or in high, cold towers,
asking questions of the stars.

559
00:48:55,683 --> 00:48:59,471
And so the people of Gondor
fell into ruin.

560
00:49:00,438 --> 00:49:02,770
The line of kings failed.

561
00:49:03,482 --> 00:49:05,848
The White Tree withered.

562
00:49:06,569 --> 00:49:10,733
The rule of Gondor was given over
to lesser men.

563
00:49:21,459 --> 00:49:22,699
Mordor.

564
00:49:23,210 --> 00:49:26,873
Yes, there it lies.

565
00:49:27,715 --> 00:49:31,048
This city has dwelt ever
in the sight of its shadow.

566
00:49:31,260 --> 00:49:32,875
[THUNDER ROLLING]

567
00:49:33,053 --> 00:49:34,714
A storm is coming.

568
00:49:35,389 --> 00:49:38,301
This is not the weather of the world.

569
00:49:38,476 --> 00:49:40,683
This is a device of Sauron's making.

570
00:49:40,853 --> 00:49:44,596
A broil of fume
he sends ahead of his host.

571
00:49:45,191 --> 00:49:47,648
The Orcs of Mordor
have no love of daylight...

572
00:49:47,818 --> 00:49:49,649
...so he covers the face of the sun...

573
00:49:49,820 --> 00:49:53,563
...to ease their passage
along the road to war.

574
00:49:53,741 --> 00:49:57,029
When the Shadow of Mordor
reaches this city...

575
00:49:57,745 --> 00:49:59,451
...it will begin.

576
00:50:01,123 --> 00:50:02,704
Well...

577
00:50:03,083 --> 00:50:04,414
...Minas Tirith...

578
00:50:06,337 --> 00:50:07,702
...very impressive.

579
00:50:07,880 --> 00:50:10,542
-So where are we off to next?
-Oh, it's too late for that, Peregrin.

580
00:50:10,716 --> 00:50:12,923
There's no leaving this city.

581
00:50:15,262 --> 00:50:18,379
Help must come to us.

582
00:50:19,975 --> 00:50:22,637
SAM:
It must be getting near teatime.

583
00:50:22,811 --> 00:50:26,520
Leastways, it would be in decent places
where there is still teatime.

584
00:50:26,690 --> 00:50:30,274
We're not in decent places.

585
00:50:35,824 --> 00:50:37,064
Mr. Frodo?

586
00:50:40,120 --> 00:50:41,326
What is it?

587
00:50:43,791 --> 00:50:46,157
It's just a feeling.

588
00:50:48,587 --> 00:50:50,748
I don't think I'll be coming back.

589
00:50:55,261 --> 00:50:57,798
Yes, you will. Of course you will.

590
00:50:58,430 --> 00:51:00,295
That's just morbid thinking.

591
00:51:00,766 --> 00:51:03,223
We're going there and back again...

592
00:51:03,394 --> 00:51:05,680
...just like Mr. Bilbo.

593
00:51:06,647 --> 00:51:08,763
You'll see.

594
00:51:16,949 --> 00:51:20,567
FRODO: I think these lands
were once part of the kingdom of Gondor.

595
00:51:24,957 --> 00:51:28,996
Long ago, when there was a king.

596
00:51:49,648 --> 00:51:52,481
Mr. Frodo, look.

597
00:51:54,111 --> 00:51:56,853
The king has got a crown again.

598
00:52:08,000 --> 00:52:12,243
Come on, Hobbits!
Mustn't stop now. This way.

599
00:52:18,969 --> 00:52:21,210
[THUNDER RUMBLING IN DISTANCE]

600
00:52:23,807 --> 00:52:25,968
[COUGHING]

601
00:52:29,104 --> 00:52:33,143
So I imagine this is just
a ceremonial position.

602
00:52:33,317 --> 00:52:37,560
I mean, they don't actually expect me
to do any fighting.

603
00:52:38,405 --> 00:52:41,647
-Do they?
-You're in the service of the steward now.

604
00:52:41,825 --> 00:52:45,192
You'll have to do as you're told,
Peregrin Took.

605
00:52:49,249 --> 00:52:51,740
Ridiculous Hobbit.

606
00:52:52,920 --> 00:52:55,127
Guard of the Citadel.

607
00:53:03,013 --> 00:53:04,469
[GRUNTS]

608
00:53:04,640 --> 00:53:06,471
Thank you.

609
00:53:15,859 --> 00:53:18,100
There's no more stars.

610
00:53:18,612 --> 00:53:19,818
Is it time?

611
00:53:20,989 --> 00:53:22,729
Yes.

612
00:53:25,369 --> 00:53:27,030
It's so quiet.

613
00:53:28,038 --> 00:53:32,281
It's the deep breath before the plunge.

614
00:53:33,460 --> 00:53:36,327
I don't want to be in a battle...

615
00:53:37,172 --> 00:53:42,132
...but waiting on the edge of one
I can't escape is even worse.

616
00:53:45,681 --> 00:53:49,299
Is there any hope, Gandalf,
for Frodo and Sam?

617
00:53:50,644 --> 00:53:53,761
GANDALF:
There never was much hope.

618
00:53:55,733 --> 00:53:57,473
Just a fool's hope.

619
00:54:03,365 --> 00:54:06,152
Our enemy is ready.

620
00:54:06,326 --> 00:54:08,988
His full strength's gathered.

621
00:54:09,163 --> 00:54:12,655
Not only Orcs, but Men as well.

622
00:54:12,833 --> 00:54:15,870
<i>Legions of Haradrim from the south...</i>

623
00:54:16,044 --> 00:54:18,751
<i>...mercenaries from the coast.</i>

624
00:54:18,922 --> 00:54:21,504
<i>All will answer Mordor's call.</i>

625
00:54:21,675 --> 00:54:23,211
MAN:
Come on.

626
00:54:24,344 --> 00:54:27,677
This will be the end of Gondor
as we know it.

627
00:54:27,848 --> 00:54:31,215
Here the hammer stroke will fall hardest.

628
00:54:32,186 --> 00:54:36,520
If the river is taken,
if the garrison at Osgiliath falls...

629
00:54:36,690 --> 00:54:40,353
...the last defense of this city
will be gone.

630
00:54:40,527 --> 00:54:44,566
But we have the White Wizard.
That's got to count for something.

631
00:54:50,454 --> 00:54:52,035
Gandalf?

632
00:54:55,751 --> 00:54:59,414
GANDALF: <i>Sauron has yet to reveal</i>
<i>his deadliest servant...</i>

633
00:54:59,880 --> 00:55:03,714
<i>...the one who will lead</i>
<i>Mordor's armies in war.</i>

634
00:55:03,884 --> 00:55:09,049
<i>The one they say no living man can kill.</i>

635
00:55:10,057 --> 00:55:12,218
The Witch-king of Angmar.

636
00:55:13,310 --> 00:55:15,676
You've met him before.

637
00:55:16,355 --> 00:55:18,937
He stabbed Frodo on Weathertop.

638
00:55:22,319 --> 00:55:24,401
[SCREAMS]

639
00:55:25,489 --> 00:55:28,196
He is the lord of the Nazgûl...

640
00:55:28,659 --> 00:55:31,116
<i>...the greatest of the Nine.</i>

641
00:55:31,286 --> 00:55:34,824
<i>Minas Morgul is his lair.</i>

642
00:55:38,377 --> 00:55:41,915
GOLLUM:
The Dead City.

643
00:55:42,089 --> 00:55:47,300
Very nasty place. Full of enemies.

644
00:55:54,518 --> 00:55:56,679
Quick. Quick.

645
00:55:56,854 --> 00:56:00,847
They will see. They will see.

646
00:56:10,117 --> 00:56:15,407
Come away. Come away.
Look, we have found it.

647
00:56:15,581 --> 00:56:19,449
The way into Mordor.

648
00:56:19,626 --> 00:56:23,960
The secret stair.

649
00:56:24,381 --> 00:56:26,747
Climb.

650
00:56:32,931 --> 00:56:35,638
[FRODO BREATHING HEAVILY]

651
00:56:44,192 --> 00:56:46,683
[VOICES WHISPERING INDISTINCTLY]

652
00:56:47,029 --> 00:56:49,771
-No, Mr. Frodo!
-Not that way!

653
00:56:50,198 --> 00:56:51,688
[GOLLUM YELLS]

654
00:56:54,620 --> 00:56:57,487
GOLLUM: What's it doing?
-No.

655
00:56:57,664 --> 00:57:00,747
-They're calling me.
GOLLUM: No.

656
00:57:01,710 --> 00:57:03,575
[RUMBLING]

657
00:57:07,174 --> 00:57:09,335
[GOLLUM SCREAMING]

658
00:57:30,405 --> 00:57:33,363
GOLLUM:
Hide! Hide!

659
00:57:47,089 --> 00:57:48,750
[GRUNTS]

660
00:57:52,594 --> 00:57:55,427
[THUNDER ROLLING]

661
00:58:01,061 --> 00:58:03,643
[ROARS]

662
00:58:08,735 --> 00:58:11,477
[WITCH-KING SCREECHING]

663
00:58:16,910 --> 00:58:19,743
I can feel his blade.

664
00:58:31,425 --> 00:58:33,541
We come to it at last.

665
00:58:35,387 --> 00:58:38,254
The great battle of our time.

666
00:59:05,792 --> 00:59:08,283
[FELL BEAST ROARS]

667
00:59:12,132 --> 00:59:14,248
[WITCH-KING SCREECHES]

668
00:59:17,429 --> 00:59:20,671
Come away, Hobbits.
We climb. We must climb.

669
00:59:30,567 --> 00:59:33,559
The board is set.

670
00:59:33,737 --> 00:59:36,103
The pieces are moving.

671
00:59:38,825 --> 00:59:41,487
Up, up, up the stairs we go.

672
00:59:41,661 --> 00:59:44,323
And then it's into the tunnel.

673
00:59:44,498 --> 00:59:47,706
Hey, what's in this tunnel?

674
00:59:48,251 --> 00:59:50,993
You listen to me,
and you listen good and proper.

675
00:59:51,171 --> 00:59:54,083
Anything happens to him,
you have me to answer to.

676
00:59:54,257 --> 00:59:55,838
One sniff something's not right...

677
00:59:56,009 --> 00:59:59,172
...one hair stands up
on the back of my head, it's over.

678
00:59:59,387 --> 01:00:02,049
No more slinker. No more stinker.

679
01:00:02,390 --> 01:00:05,006
You're gone. Got it?

680
01:00:05,894 --> 01:00:07,885
I'm watching you.

681
01:00:13,235 --> 01:00:15,226
What was that about?

682
01:00:15,403 --> 01:00:17,815
Nothing. Just clearing something up.

683
01:00:24,454 --> 01:00:27,321
Peregrin Took, my lad,
there is a task now to be done.

684
01:00:27,499 --> 01:00:32,084
Another opportunity for one
of the Shire-folk to prove their great worth.

685
01:00:36,925 --> 01:00:38,506
You must not fail me.

686
01:01:12,752 --> 01:01:15,835
MADRIL:
It's been very quiet across the river.

687
01:01:16,006 --> 01:01:18,338
The Orcs are lying low.

688
01:01:18,508 --> 01:01:20,499
The garrison may have moved out.

689
01:01:21,636 --> 01:01:24,343
We've sent scouts to Cair Andros.

690
01:01:24,514 --> 01:01:26,800
If the Orcs attack from the north,
we'll have some warning.

691
01:01:51,625 --> 01:01:52,956
[OAR SPLASHES]

692
01:01:53,126 --> 01:01:54,332
Quiet.

693
01:01:58,423 --> 01:02:00,379
SOLDIER:
We need 10 more.

694
01:02:00,675 --> 01:02:03,792
[SOLDIERS SPEAKING
INDISTINCTLY]

695
01:02:21,696 --> 01:02:23,232
Kill him!

696
01:02:40,548 --> 01:02:42,960
They're not coming from the north.

697
01:02:44,386 --> 01:02:48,720
-To the river. Quick. Quick.
-Go. Come on.

698
01:02:52,185 --> 01:02:53,766
Faster.

699
01:03:06,908 --> 01:03:09,274
Draw swords.

700
01:03:54,289 --> 01:03:56,371
[YELLING]

701
01:04:03,840 --> 01:04:06,422
FARAMIR:
Hold! Hold them!

702
01:05:26,714 --> 01:05:28,579
What?

703
01:05:41,146 --> 01:05:42,556
Amon Dîn.

704
01:05:48,361 --> 01:05:51,398
GUARD: The beacon.
The beacon of Amon Dîn is lit.

705
01:05:54,659 --> 01:05:58,868
Hope is kindled.

706
01:07:31,256 --> 01:07:35,625
ARAGORN: The beacons of Minas Tirith!
The beacons are lit!

707
01:07:36,844 --> 01:07:38,459
Gondor calls for aid.

708
01:07:48,982 --> 01:07:51,894
And Rohan will answer.

709
01:07:52,318 --> 01:07:55,105
Muster the Rohirrim.

710
01:07:58,992 --> 01:08:01,483
[BELL RINGING]

711
01:08:10,211 --> 01:08:12,167
Assemble the army at Dunharrow.

712
01:08:12,338 --> 01:08:16,707
As many men as can be found.
You have two days.

713
01:08:16,884 --> 01:08:22,174
On the third,
we ride for Gondor and war.

714
01:08:22,682 --> 01:08:24,343
MAN 1: Forward.
MAN 2: Very good, sir.

715
01:08:24,517 --> 01:08:25,927
-Gamling.
GAMLING: My lord.

716
01:08:26,102 --> 01:08:27,717
Make haste
across the Riddermark.

717
01:08:27,895 --> 01:08:30,011
Summon every able-bodied man
to Dunharrow.

718
01:08:30,189 --> 01:08:31,770
GAMLING:
I will.

719
01:08:35,862 --> 01:08:39,025
-Will you ride with us?
-Just to the encampment.

720
01:08:39,198 --> 01:08:43,111
It's tradition for the women
of the court to farewell the men.

721
01:08:49,667 --> 01:08:51,578
The men have found their captain.

722
01:08:51,753 --> 01:08:55,086
They will follow you into battle,
even to death.

723
01:08:55,256 --> 01:08:56,837
You have given us hope.

724
01:09:00,053 --> 01:09:02,009
MERRY:
Excuse me.

725
01:09:03,348 --> 01:09:04,838
I have a sword.

726
01:09:05,141 --> 01:09:06,506
Please accept it.

727
01:09:07,644 --> 01:09:12,138
I offer you my service, Théoden King.

728
01:09:15,568 --> 01:09:17,650
And gladly I accept it.

729
01:09:18,738 --> 01:09:22,822
You shall be Meriadoc,
esquire of Rohan.

730
01:09:27,705 --> 01:09:28,911
Horse-Men.

731
01:09:29,582 --> 01:09:35,202
I wish I could muster a legion of Dwarves,
fully armed and filthy.

732
01:09:35,588 --> 01:09:38,546
Your kinsmen may have no need
to ride to war.

733
01:09:38,716 --> 01:09:42,129
I fear war already marches
on their own lands.

734
01:10:00,613 --> 01:10:04,071
THÉODEN: <i>So it is before the walls</i>
<i>of Minas Tirith...</i>

735
01:10:04,242 --> 01:10:08,110
<i>...the doom of our time will be decided.</i>

736
01:10:10,707 --> 01:10:16,247
Now is the hour.
Riders of Rohan, oaths you have taken.

737
01:10:16,421 --> 01:10:20,790
Now, fulfill them all.
To lord and land! Hyah!

738
01:11:03,050 --> 01:11:05,006
Faramir!

739
01:11:11,309 --> 01:11:15,018
We can't hold them. The city is lost.

740
01:11:15,605 --> 01:11:18,688
Tell the men to break cover.
We ride for Minas Tirith.

741
01:11:23,529 --> 01:11:27,272
[RINGWRAITHS SCREECHING]

742
01:11:27,450 --> 01:11:29,691
Nazgûl.

743
01:11:32,079 --> 01:11:34,536
SOLDIER 1:
Take cover!

744
01:11:34,707 --> 01:11:37,244
SOLDIER 2:
Nazgûl!

745
01:11:37,418 --> 01:11:41,081
Fall back. Fall back to Minas Tirith!

746
01:11:47,678 --> 01:11:49,543
Fall back!

747
01:11:56,604 --> 01:12:01,189
-Retreat! Retreat!
SOLDIER 3: Run for your lives!

748
01:12:02,151 --> 01:12:04,233
[GASPING]

749
01:12:18,251 --> 01:12:19,707
[GRUNTS]

750
01:12:22,046 --> 01:12:24,128
[SIGHS]

751
01:12:25,424 --> 01:12:29,758
The age of Men is over.

752
01:12:29,929 --> 01:12:35,549
The time of the Orc has come.

753
01:12:37,937 --> 01:12:40,269
SOLDIER 1: Keep going.
SOLDIER 2: It's the Nazgûl.

754
01:12:41,899 --> 01:12:44,265
SOLDIER 1:
Take cover, my lord!

755
01:12:44,569 --> 01:12:45,900
It's coming!

756
01:12:46,070 --> 01:12:48,152
[YELLING INDISTINCTLY]

757
01:12:51,450 --> 01:12:54,817
MAN: It's Mithrandir.
-The White Rider!

758
01:13:00,668 --> 01:13:02,533
[SCREAMS]

759
01:13:34,785 --> 01:13:36,150
GUARD:
Pull!

760
01:13:53,888 --> 01:13:56,300
FARAMIR:
Mithrandir.

761
01:13:56,474 --> 01:13:58,214
They broke through our defenses.

762
01:13:58,392 --> 01:14:00,599
They've taken the bridge
and the west bank.

763
01:14:01,687 --> 01:14:03,678
Battalions of Orcs are crossing the river.

764
01:14:03,856 --> 01:14:05,847
IORLAS:
It is as the Lord Denethor predicted.

765
01:14:06,025 --> 01:14:10,564
-Long has he foreseen this doom.
-Foreseen and done nothing.

766
01:14:13,950 --> 01:14:16,362
Faramir?

767
01:14:18,287 --> 01:14:22,121
This is not the first Halfling
to have crossed your path.

768
01:14:22,291 --> 01:14:24,498
No.

769
01:14:25,836 --> 01:14:27,372
You've seen Frodo and Sam?

770
01:14:28,255 --> 01:14:31,668
-Where? When?
-In Ithilien.

771
01:14:31,842 --> 01:14:33,924
Not two days ago.

772
01:14:34,387 --> 01:14:38,847
Gandalf, they're taking the road
to the Morgul Vale.

773
01:14:39,558 --> 01:14:42,174
And then the pass of Cirith Ungol.

774
01:14:44,397 --> 01:14:46,763
What does that mean?

775
01:14:46,941 --> 01:14:51,856
-What's wrong?
-Faramir, tell me everything.

776
01:14:52,029 --> 01:14:54,065
Tell me all you know.

777
01:14:55,241 --> 01:14:58,654
This is how you would serve your city?

778
01:14:58,828 --> 01:15:02,116
You would risk its utter ruin?

779
01:15:03,165 --> 01:15:04,746
I did what I judged to be right.

780
01:15:05,459 --> 01:15:08,451
What you judged to be right.

781
01:15:09,088 --> 01:15:14,958
You sent the Ring of Power into Mordor
in the hands of a witless Halfling.

782
01:15:18,931 --> 01:15:23,766
It should have been brought back
to the Citadel to be kept safe.

783
01:15:25,396 --> 01:15:26,932
Hidden.

784
01:15:27,356 --> 01:15:30,098
Dark and deep in the vaults...

785
01:15:30,276 --> 01:15:32,437
...not to be used.

786
01:15:36,615 --> 01:15:41,484
Unless at the uttermost end of need.

787
01:15:41,954 --> 01:15:43,990
I would not use the Ring.

788
01:15:44,165 --> 01:15:47,248
Not if Minas Tirith were falling in ruin
and I alone could save her.

789
01:15:47,585 --> 01:15:52,420
Ever you desire to appear lordly
and gracious...

790
01:15:52,590 --> 01:15:54,831
...as a king of old.

791
01:15:56,635 --> 01:16:00,378
Boromir would have remembered
his father's need.

792
01:16:00,806 --> 01:16:03,263
He would have brought me a kingly gift.

793
01:16:03,476 --> 01:16:06,013
Boromir would not
have brought the Ring.

794
01:16:06,437 --> 01:16:09,554
He would have stretched out his hand to
this thing and taken it. He would've fallen.

795
01:16:09,732 --> 01:16:11,973
-You know nothing of this matter!
-He would have kept it for his own.

796
01:16:13,861 --> 01:16:16,022
And when he returned...

797
01:16:17,156 --> 01:16:18,817
...you would not have known your son.

798
01:16:18,991 --> 01:16:21,528
Boromir was loyal to me!

799
01:16:21,702 --> 01:16:24,284
Not some wizard's pupil!

800
01:16:24,663 --> 01:16:26,745
[WHIMPERS]

801
01:16:32,421 --> 01:16:33,752
Father?

802
01:16:46,435 --> 01:16:48,346
My son.

803
01:17:14,588 --> 01:17:15,953
Leave me.

804
01:17:46,370 --> 01:17:47,826
[GRUNTS]

805
01:17:49,540 --> 01:17:52,077
GOLLUM:
Careful, master. Careful.

806
01:17:52,418 --> 01:17:55,330
Very far to fall.

807
01:17:57,840 --> 01:18:01,753
Very dangerous are the stairs.

808
01:18:04,430 --> 01:18:06,967
Come, master.

809
01:18:12,771 --> 01:18:15,934
Come to Sméagol.

810
01:18:22,281 --> 01:18:23,771
SAM:
Mr. Frodo.

811
01:18:24,783 --> 01:18:26,319
Get back, you!

812
01:18:26,493 --> 01:18:28,700
Don't touch him!

813
01:18:32,833 --> 01:18:35,666
Why does he hates poor Sméagol?

814
01:18:35,836 --> 01:18:39,545
What has Sméagol ever done to him?

815
01:18:39,715 --> 01:18:41,046
Master?

816
01:18:41,217 --> 01:18:42,707
[PANTING]

817
01:18:42,885 --> 01:18:46,343
Master carries heavy burden.

818
01:18:46,513 --> 01:18:51,928
Sméagol knows.
Heavy, heavy burden.

819
01:18:52,102 --> 01:18:55,344
Fat one cannot know.

820
01:18:57,399 --> 01:19:00,141
Sméagol look after master.

821
01:19:01,362 --> 01:19:03,569
He wants it.

822
01:19:03,739 --> 01:19:08,278
He needs it.
Sméagol sees it in his eye.

823
01:19:08,452 --> 01:19:13,913
Very soon he will ask you for it.
You will see.

824
01:19:14,083 --> 01:19:17,951
The fat one will take it from you.

825
01:19:25,177 --> 01:19:29,511
WITCH-KING:
Send forth all legions.

826
01:19:29,682 --> 01:19:33,721
Do not stop the attack
until the city is taken.

827
01:19:34,436 --> 01:19:37,553
Slay them all.

828
01:19:39,233 --> 01:19:45,024
-What of the wizard?
WITCH-KING: I will break him.

829
01:19:48,367 --> 01:19:50,779
GUARD:
Where are Théoden's riders?

830
01:19:50,953 --> 01:19:53,535
Will Rohan's army come?

831
01:19:53,706 --> 01:19:55,947
Mithrandir.

832
01:19:57,001 --> 01:20:00,869
Courage is the best defense
that you have now.

833
01:20:05,676 --> 01:20:08,383
PIPPIN:
What were you thinking, Peregrin Took?

834
01:20:10,472 --> 01:20:16,183
What service can a Hobbit
offer such a great lord of Men?

835
01:20:16,353 --> 01:20:17,843
FARAMIR:
It was well-done.

836
01:20:21,025 --> 01:20:25,064
A generous deed should not
be checked with cold counsel.

837
01:20:25,821 --> 01:20:28,358
You are to join the tower guard.

838
01:20:28,907 --> 01:20:31,899
I didn't think they would find any livery
that would fit me.

839
01:20:32,077 --> 01:20:34,534
Once belonged to a young boy
of the city.

840
01:20:34,705 --> 01:20:36,241
A very foolish one...

841
01:20:36,415 --> 01:20:40,658
...who wasted many hours slaying dragons
instead of attending to his studies.

842
01:20:40,836 --> 01:20:43,578
-This was yours?
-Yes, it was mine.

843
01:20:43,756 --> 01:20:45,542
My father had it made for me.

844
01:20:46,592 --> 01:20:47,923
Well...

845
01:20:48,093 --> 01:20:50,084
...I'm taller than you were then.

846
01:20:50,262 --> 01:20:53,595
Though I'm not likely to grow anymore,
except sideways.

847
01:20:53,807 --> 01:20:56,014
[LAUGHING]

848
01:20:56,560 --> 01:20:58,596
Never fitted me either.

849
01:20:58,771 --> 01:21:01,604
Boromir was always the soldier.

850
01:21:04,610 --> 01:21:07,022
They were so alike, he and my father.

851
01:21:09,114 --> 01:21:10,729
Proud.

852
01:21:10,908 --> 01:21:12,114
Stubborn even.

853
01:21:13,869 --> 01:21:15,359
But strong.

854
01:21:16,872 --> 01:21:20,035
I think you have strength
of a different kind.

855
01:21:20,667 --> 01:21:23,124
And one day your father will see it.

856
01:21:27,299 --> 01:21:31,087
PIPPIN: Here do I swear fealty
and service to Gondor...

857
01:21:31,261 --> 01:21:32,751
...in peace or war...

858
01:21:33,389 --> 01:21:35,846
...in living or dying...

859
01:21:37,226 --> 01:21:38,466
...from....

860
01:21:41,146 --> 01:21:43,933
From this hour henceforth...

861
01:21:44,108 --> 01:21:46,019
...until my lord release me...

862
01:21:47,528 --> 01:21:49,735
...or death take me.

863
01:21:50,322 --> 01:21:52,813
And I shall not forget it...

864
01:21:52,991 --> 01:21:56,358
...nor fail to reward
that which is given.

865
01:22:03,961 --> 01:22:06,247
Fealty with love.

866
01:22:07,339 --> 01:22:09,000
Valor with honor.

867
01:22:10,592 --> 01:22:13,925
Disloyalty with vengeance.

868
01:22:22,563 --> 01:22:26,647
I do not think we should so lightly
abandon the outer defenses...

869
01:22:26,817 --> 01:22:29,559
...defenses that your brother
long held intact.

870
01:22:29,736 --> 01:22:32,227
-What would you have me do?
-I will not yield...

871
01:22:32,406 --> 01:22:35,193
...the river in Pelennor unfought.

872
01:22:35,367 --> 01:22:37,028
Osgiliath must be retaken.

873
01:22:37,202 --> 01:22:39,238
My lord, Osgiliath is overrun.

874
01:22:39,913 --> 01:22:42,700
Much must be risked in war.

875
01:22:45,335 --> 01:22:49,294
Is there a captain here who still has
the courage to do his lord's will?

876
01:22:55,512 --> 01:22:58,754
You wish now that our places
had been exchanged...

877
01:22:59,725 --> 01:23:02,558
...that I had died
and Boromir had lived.

878
01:23:05,981 --> 01:23:07,721
Yes.

879
01:23:08,400 --> 01:23:10,607
I wish that.

880
01:23:18,994 --> 01:23:21,485
Since you were robbed
of Boromir...

881
01:23:23,332 --> 01:23:26,244
...I will do what I can
in his stead.

882
01:23:34,426 --> 01:23:38,886
If I should return,
think better of me, Father.

883
01:23:40,974 --> 01:23:44,592
That will depend on the manner
of your return.

884
01:23:51,318 --> 01:23:53,400
[SNORING]

885
01:24:44,037 --> 01:24:45,868
Ugh.

886
01:25:07,894 --> 01:25:10,226
SAM:
What are you up to?

887
01:25:10,397 --> 01:25:11,637
Sneaking off, are we?

888
01:25:12,357 --> 01:25:14,188
Sneaking?

889
01:25:15,193 --> 01:25:17,354
Sneaking?

890
01:25:18,780 --> 01:25:21,943
Fat Hobbit is always so polite.

891
01:25:22,117 --> 01:25:27,202
Sméagol shows them secret ways
that nobody else could find...

892
01:25:27,372 --> 01:25:29,533
...and they say "sneak."

893
01:25:30,167 --> 01:25:32,749
Sneak?

894
01:25:33,378 --> 01:25:36,085
Very nice friend.
Oh, yes, my precious.

895
01:25:36,256 --> 01:25:38,872
-Very nice, very nice.
-All right. All right!

896
01:25:40,135 --> 01:25:42,342
You just startled me is all.

897
01:25:42,846 --> 01:25:44,677
What were you doing?

898
01:25:46,308 --> 01:25:48,424
Sneaking.

899
01:25:48,810 --> 01:25:51,893
Fine. Have it your own way.

900
01:25:54,149 --> 01:25:56,640
I'm sorry to wake you, Mr. Frodo.

901
01:25:57,027 --> 01:25:58,983
We have to be moving on.

902
01:26:04,159 --> 01:26:05,740
It's dark still.

903
01:26:05,911 --> 01:26:08,118
It's always dark here.

904
01:26:12,376 --> 01:26:14,287
It's gone!

905
01:26:15,504 --> 01:26:18,371
-The Elven bread.
-What?

906
01:26:18,548 --> 01:26:20,004
That's all we have left.

907
01:26:20,175 --> 01:26:22,257
[GOLLUM BREATHING UNEVENLY]

908
01:26:24,096 --> 01:26:26,587
He took it. He must have!

909
01:26:27,099 --> 01:26:30,341
Sméagol?
No, no, not poor Sméagol.

910
01:26:30,519 --> 01:26:33,431
Sméagol hates nasty Elf bread.

911
01:26:33,605 --> 01:26:36,768
You're a lying rat!
What did you do with it?!

912
01:26:36,942 --> 01:26:38,478
He doesn't eat it.

913
01:26:39,486 --> 01:26:41,818
-He can't have taken it.
GOLLUM: Look.

914
01:26:42,864 --> 01:26:44,695
What's this?

915
01:26:47,369 --> 01:26:50,702
Crumbs on his jacketses.
He took it!

916
01:26:51,415 --> 01:26:53,076
He took it.

917
01:26:53,917 --> 01:26:58,126
I seen him. He's always stuffing
his face when master's not looking.

918
01:26:58,296 --> 01:27:00,082
That's a filthy lie!

919
01:27:00,257 --> 01:27:02,464
You stinking, two-faced sneak!

920
01:27:02,634 --> 01:27:03,874
-Sam!
SAM: Call me--

921
01:27:04,052 --> 01:27:05,292
FRODO:
Stop it!

922
01:27:05,470 --> 01:27:06,755
[GOLLUM YELLS]

923
01:27:06,930 --> 01:27:08,636
Sam!

924
01:27:08,807 --> 01:27:12,425
-I'll kill him!
-Sam! No!

925
01:27:13,478 --> 01:27:19,018
Oh, my-- I'm sorry. I didn't mean it
to go so far. I was just so-- So angry.

926
01:27:19,192 --> 01:27:21,308
Here, just--
Let's just rest a bit.

927
01:27:21,486 --> 01:27:23,568
-I'm all right.
-No.

928
01:27:23,739 --> 01:27:26,822
No, you're not all right.
You're exhausted.

929
01:27:26,992 --> 01:27:29,108
It's that Gollum.

930
01:27:29,286 --> 01:27:30,992
It's this place.

931
01:27:31,163 --> 01:27:33,745
It's that thing around your neck.

932
01:27:37,252 --> 01:27:38,537
I could help a bit.

933
01:27:38,712 --> 01:27:41,374
I could carry it for a while.

934
01:27:41,548 --> 01:27:43,288
[VOICE ECHOING]
Carry it for a while.

935
01:27:43,467 --> 01:27:44,707
I could carry it...I could carry it.

936
01:27:45,343 --> 01:27:50,804
Share the load...Share the load...
the load...the load.

937
01:27:50,974 --> 01:27:52,180
Get away!

938
01:27:52,350 --> 01:27:53,931
[IN NORMAL VOICE]
I don't want to keep it.

939
01:27:57,522 --> 01:27:59,513
I just want to help.

940
01:28:01,568 --> 01:28:04,184
See? See?

941
01:28:04,362 --> 01:28:07,775
He wants it for himself.

942
01:28:07,949 --> 01:28:09,655
Shut up, you!

943
01:28:10,202 --> 01:28:12,033
Go away!
Get out of here!

944
01:28:12,204 --> 01:28:14,035
FRODO:
No, Sam.

945
01:28:14,206 --> 01:28:15,446
It's you.

946
01:28:19,669 --> 01:28:21,375
I'm sorry, Sam.

947
01:28:23,048 --> 01:28:24,413
But he's a liar.

948
01:28:24,591 --> 01:28:27,253
He's poisoned you against me.

949
01:28:28,678 --> 01:28:30,589
You can't help me anymore.

950
01:28:32,557 --> 01:28:34,422
You don't mean that.

951
01:28:36,937 --> 01:28:38,723
Go home.

952
01:28:51,117 --> 01:28:53,403
[SOBBING]

953
01:29:58,768 --> 01:30:00,554
GANDALF:
Faramir!

954
01:30:00,729 --> 01:30:02,640
Faramir!

955
01:30:04,149 --> 01:30:06,185
Your father's will has turned
to madness.

956
01:30:07,360 --> 01:30:09,396
Do not throw away your life
so rashly.

957
01:30:10,155 --> 01:30:12,487
Where does my allegiance lie
if not here?

958
01:30:13,116 --> 01:30:16,028
This is the city of the Men of Númenor.

959
01:30:16,661 --> 01:30:19,448
I will gladly give my life
to defend her beauty...

960
01:30:19,623 --> 01:30:22,831
...her memory, her wisdom.

961
01:30:25,211 --> 01:30:28,624
Your father loves you, Faramir.

962
01:30:29,341 --> 01:30:32,333
He will remember it
before the end.

963
01:31:14,970 --> 01:31:17,382
[HORSES WHINNYING]

964
01:31:41,955 --> 01:31:43,491
Can you sing, Master Hobbit?

965
01:31:46,376 --> 01:31:47,866
Well...

966
01:31:48,420 --> 01:31:50,035
...yes.

967
01:31:50,755 --> 01:31:54,498
At least, well enough
for my own people.

968
01:31:56,136 --> 01:31:58,548
But we have no songs
for great halls...

969
01:31:59,597 --> 01:32:00,837
...and evil times.

970
01:32:01,683 --> 01:32:04,846
And why should your songs
be unfit for my halls?

971
01:32:07,647 --> 01:32:09,057
Come, sing me a song.

972
01:32:12,318 --> 01:32:13,649
[CHEWING NOISILY]

973
01:32:20,118 --> 01:32:23,451
[SINGING]
<i>Home is behind</i>

974
01:32:23,621 --> 01:32:27,364
<i>The world ahead</i>

975
01:32:29,794 --> 01:32:35,630
<i>And there are many paths to tread</i>

976
01:32:37,427 --> 01:32:40,965
<i>Through shadow</i>

977
01:32:41,139 --> 01:32:45,303
<i>To the edge of night</i>

978
01:32:46,978 --> 01:32:52,063
<i>Until the stars are all alight</i>

979
01:32:55,070 --> 01:32:59,404
<i>Mist and shadow</i>

980
01:32:59,574 --> 01:33:03,863
<i>Cloud and shade</i>

981
01:33:06,247 --> 01:33:09,580
<i>All shall fade</i>

982
01:33:11,961 --> 01:33:15,954
<i>All shall</i>

983
01:33:16,174 --> 01:33:17,584
[VOICE MUTED]

984
01:33:21,721 --> 01:33:24,087
<i>Fade</i>

985
01:33:37,153 --> 01:33:38,689
[BELL TOLLING IN DISTANCE]

986
01:33:48,498 --> 01:33:51,956
LEAD ORC:
March! March!

987
01:33:52,127 --> 01:33:57,247
March! March! March!

988
01:34:00,802 --> 01:34:03,134
MAN 1:
Make way for the king.

989
01:34:04,639 --> 01:34:06,630
Make way.

990
01:34:09,102 --> 01:34:11,138
MAN 2:
The king is here.

991
01:34:13,106 --> 01:34:14,721
MAN 3:
My lord.

992
01:34:15,984 --> 01:34:17,940
MAN 4:
Hail to you, sire.

993
01:34:18,403 --> 01:34:19,609
Grimbold, how many?

994
01:34:19,779 --> 01:34:22,236
I bring 500 men from the Westfold,
my lord.

995
01:34:23,199 --> 01:34:25,861
FENMARCH MAN: We have 300 more
from Fenmarch, Théoden King.

996
01:34:26,995 --> 01:34:30,954
-Where are the riders from Snowbourn?
GAMLING: None have come, my lord.

997
01:34:48,016 --> 01:34:50,132
THÉODEN:
Six thousand spears.

998
01:34:51,186 --> 01:34:53,177
Less than half of what I'd hoped for.

999
01:34:53,479 --> 01:34:56,846
Six thousand will not be enough
to break the lines of Mordor.

1000
01:34:59,611 --> 01:35:01,351
More will come.

1001
01:35:01,738 --> 01:35:04,696
Every hour lost hastens Gondor's defeat.

1002
01:35:04,866 --> 01:35:07,448
We have till dawn,
then we must ride.

1003
01:35:12,582 --> 01:35:15,073
[HORSES WHINNYING]

1004
01:35:26,930 --> 01:35:29,262
The horses are restless...

1005
01:35:29,432 --> 01:35:30,922
...and the men are quiet.

1006
01:35:31,392 --> 01:35:34,509
They grow nervous in the shadow
of the mountain.

1007
01:35:36,981 --> 01:35:38,846
GIMLI:
That road there...

1008
01:35:39,776 --> 01:35:41,858
...where does that lead?

1009
01:35:42,612 --> 01:35:46,446
It is the road to the Dimholt,
the door under the mountain.

1010
01:35:47,158 --> 01:35:50,150
None who venture there ever return.

1011
01:35:51,371 --> 01:35:53,236
That mountain is evil.

1012
01:35:58,628 --> 01:36:00,744
[HORSE WHINNIES]

1013
01:36:04,592 --> 01:36:06,674
MAN:
Hold!

1014
01:36:09,472 --> 01:36:12,179
[DEEP RUMBLING]

1015
01:36:16,187 --> 01:36:18,018
GIMLI:
Aragorn.

1016
01:36:18,773 --> 01:36:20,684
Let's find some food.

1017
01:36:37,208 --> 01:36:38,618
There.

1018
01:36:39,544 --> 01:36:42,536
A true esquire of Rohan.

1019
01:36:46,217 --> 01:36:47,878
I'm ready.

1020
01:36:48,052 --> 01:36:49,633
[LAUGHS]

1021
01:36:49,804 --> 01:36:51,044
Sorry.

1022
01:36:51,222 --> 01:36:53,508
It isn't all that dangerous.

1023
01:36:54,017 --> 01:36:56,349
It's not even sharp.

1024
01:36:57,020 --> 01:37:00,387
Well, that's no good. You won't kill
many Orcs with a blunt blade.

1025
01:37:00,565 --> 01:37:02,055
Come on.

1026
01:37:06,237 --> 01:37:08,728
To the smithy. Go!

1027
01:37:10,241 --> 01:37:12,732
You should not encourage him.

1028
01:37:12,952 --> 01:37:15,409
You should not doubt him.

1029
01:37:15,580 --> 01:37:18,868
I do not doubt his heart,
only the reach of his arm.

1030
01:37:19,083 --> 01:37:20,448
[SNICKERS]

1031
01:37:21,586 --> 01:37:23,167
Why should Merry be left behind?

1032
01:37:23,338 --> 01:37:25,954
He has as much cause
to go to war as you.

1033
01:37:28,092 --> 01:37:31,255
Why can he not fight
for those he loves?

1034
01:37:34,557 --> 01:37:37,549
You know as little of war
as that Hobbit.

1035
01:37:38,770 --> 01:37:40,886
When the fear takes him...

1036
01:37:41,064 --> 01:37:46,104
...and the blood and the screams
and the horror of battle take hold...

1037
01:37:46,486 --> 01:37:48,602
...do you think he would stand and fight?

1038
01:37:51,199 --> 01:37:52,780
He would flee.

1039
01:37:52,992 --> 01:37:55,028
And he would be right to do so.

1040
01:37:57,246 --> 01:38:01,205
War is the province of Men, Éowyn.

1041
01:38:23,940 --> 01:38:26,022
[RUMBLING]

1042
01:38:26,984 --> 01:38:29,100
[WIND WHISTLING]

1043
01:38:36,828 --> 01:38:40,571
ARWEN:
<i>I choose a mortal life.</i>

1044
01:38:43,501 --> 01:38:46,334
I wish I could've seen him...

1045
01:38:47,505 --> 01:38:50,167
...one last time.

1046
01:38:59,100 --> 01:39:00,965
[GRUNTS]

1047
01:39:01,352 --> 01:39:02,808
MAN:
Sir?

1048
01:39:04,647 --> 01:39:07,184
King Théoden awaits you, my lord.

1049
01:39:28,004 --> 01:39:29,960
I take my leave.

1050
01:39:44,604 --> 01:39:45,844
My lord Elrond.

1051
01:39:46,397 --> 01:39:49,889
I come on behalf of one whom I love.

1052
01:39:53,029 --> 01:39:55,020
Arwen is dying.

1053
01:39:59,827 --> 01:40:03,866
She will not long survive the evil
that now spreads from Mordor.

1054
01:40:04,624 --> 01:40:07,991
The light of the Evenstar is failing.

1055
01:40:08,169 --> 01:40:12,162
As Sauron's power grows,
her strength wanes.

1056
01:40:12,340 --> 01:40:16,083
Arwen's life is now tied
to the fate of the Ring.

1057
01:40:16,844 --> 01:40:19,426
The Shadow is upon us, Aragorn.

1058
01:40:19,764 --> 01:40:21,425
The end has come.

1059
01:40:21,849 --> 01:40:24,431
It will not be our end, but his.

1060
01:40:25,228 --> 01:40:28,766
You ride to war, but not to victory.

1061
01:40:29,774 --> 01:40:33,437
Sauron's armies march on Minas Tirith,
this you know.

1062
01:40:33,653 --> 01:40:38,067
But in secret he sends another force
which will attack from the river.

1063
01:40:38,533 --> 01:40:41,946
<i>A fleet of Corsair ships sails</i>
<i>from the south.</i>

1064
01:40:42,578 --> 01:40:44,660
They'll be in the city in two days.

1065
01:40:45,164 --> 01:40:47,951
You're outnumbered, Aragorn.

1066
01:40:48,709 --> 01:40:50,791
You need more men.

1067
01:40:51,212 --> 01:40:52,952
There are none.

1068
01:40:54,715 --> 01:40:58,628
There are those who dwell
in the mountain.

1069
01:40:59,053 --> 01:41:01,169
[EERIE BREATHING,
WIND WHISTLING]

1070
01:41:07,645 --> 01:41:09,806
Murderers...

1071
01:41:09,981 --> 01:41:11,391
...traitors.

1072
01:41:13,818 --> 01:41:15,979
You would call upon them to fight?

1073
01:41:16,195 --> 01:41:17,776
They believe in nothing.

1074
01:41:17,947 --> 01:41:20,063
They answer to no one.

1075
01:41:20,241 --> 01:41:23,324
They will answer
to the king of Gondor.

1076
01:41:30,459 --> 01:41:35,579
Andúril, the Flame of the West,
forged from the shards of Narsil.

1077
01:41:49,854 --> 01:41:54,314
Sauron will not have forgotten
the Sword of Elendil.

1078
01:42:08,372 --> 01:42:13,116
The blade that was broken
shall return to Minas Tirith.

1079
01:42:13,294 --> 01:42:15,706
The man who can wield
the power of this sword...

1080
01:42:15,880 --> 01:42:19,748
...can summon to him an army more
deadly than any that walks this earth.

1081
01:42:21,552 --> 01:42:23,713
Put aside the Ranger.

1082
01:42:23,888 --> 01:42:27,221
Become who you were born to be.

1083
01:42:27,391 --> 01:42:29,382
Take the Dimholt road.

1084
01:42:33,397 --> 01:42:36,230
[SPEAKING IN ELVISH]

1085
01:42:55,419 --> 01:42:57,080
Why are you doing this?

1086
01:42:57,588 --> 01:43:00,796
The war lies to the east.
You cannot leave on the eve of battle.

1087
01:43:03,219 --> 01:43:05,301
You cannot abandon the men.

1088
01:43:06,597 --> 01:43:08,178
Éowyn....

1089
01:43:08,349 --> 01:43:10,556
We need you here.

1090
01:43:11,686 --> 01:43:13,551
Why have you come?

1091
01:43:15,231 --> 01:43:17,187
Do you not know?

1092
01:43:26,450 --> 01:43:29,442
It is but a shadow and a thought
that you love.

1093
01:43:33,416 --> 01:43:35,828
I cannot give you what you seek.

1094
01:43:49,348 --> 01:43:53,261
I have wished you joy
since first I saw you.

1095
01:44:12,413 --> 01:44:14,654
GIMLI:
Just where do you think you're off to?

1096
01:44:14,874 --> 01:44:16,159
Not this time.

1097
01:44:16,375 --> 01:44:18,582
-This time you must stay, Gimli.
-Mm.

1098
01:44:21,297 --> 01:44:24,130
Have you learned nothing
of the stubbornness of Dwarves?

1099
01:44:24,300 --> 01:44:27,963
You might as well accept it.
We're going with you, laddie.

1100
01:44:38,773 --> 01:44:40,855
[MEN CHATTERING INDISTINCTLY]

1101
01:44:50,284 --> 01:44:52,445
MAN 1: What's happening?
-Where is he going?

1102
01:44:52,787 --> 01:44:54,652
Where's he going?

1103
01:44:57,208 --> 01:44:59,290
I don't understand.

1104
01:45:03,714 --> 01:45:05,500
MAN 2:
Lord Aragorn!

1105
01:45:05,925 --> 01:45:08,632
MAN 1:
Why does he leave on the eve of battle?

1106
01:45:09,845 --> 01:45:11,927
He leaves because there is no hope.

1107
01:45:12,556 --> 01:45:14,717
He leaves because he must.

1108
01:45:14,892 --> 01:45:16,553
GAMLING:
Too few have come.

1109
01:45:16,727 --> 01:45:18,934
We cannot defeat
the armies of Mordor.

1110
01:45:21,440 --> 01:45:23,055
No...

1111
01:45:23,526 --> 01:45:24,732
...we cannot.

1112
01:45:27,655 --> 01:45:31,443
But we will meet them
in battle nonetheless.

1113
01:45:45,881 --> 01:45:47,587
I have left instruction.

1114
01:45:50,261 --> 01:45:53,549
The people are to follow
your rule in my stead.

1115
01:46:00,104 --> 01:46:02,390
Take up my seat in the Golden Hall.

1116
01:46:03,607 --> 01:46:06,440
Long may you defend Edoras...

1117
01:46:06,610 --> 01:46:08,976
...if the battle goes ill.

1118
01:46:10,072 --> 01:46:13,485
What other duty would you
have me do, my lord?

1119
01:46:15,703 --> 01:46:17,614
Duty?

1120
01:46:19,790 --> 01:46:21,121
No.

1121
01:46:29,466 --> 01:46:31,582
I would have you smile again...

1122
01:46:35,014 --> 01:46:40,008
...not grieve for those
whose time has come.

1123
01:46:44,815 --> 01:46:48,307
You shall live to see
these days renewed...

1124
01:46:52,656 --> 01:46:55,443
...and no more despair.

1125
01:47:01,665 --> 01:47:05,328
GIMLI: What kind of army would linger
in such a place?

1126
01:47:05,544 --> 01:47:07,330
LEGOLAS:
One that is cursed.

1127
01:47:09,340 --> 01:47:11,831
Long ago, the Men of the Mountains
swore an oath...

1128
01:47:12,301 --> 01:47:15,043
...to the last king of Gondor...

1129
01:47:15,638 --> 01:47:17,174
...to come to his aid...

1130
01:47:17,348 --> 01:47:19,088
...to fight.

1131
01:47:19,600 --> 01:47:21,761
But when the time came...

1132
01:47:22,353 --> 01:47:25,015
...when Gondor's need was dire...

1133
01:47:25,189 --> 01:47:27,020
...they fled...

1134
01:47:27,191 --> 01:47:30,604
...vanishing into the darkness
of the mountain.

1135
01:47:31,654 --> 01:47:33,986
And so Isildur cursed them...

1136
01:47:35,532 --> 01:47:39,366
...never to rest until they had
fulfilled their pledge.

1137
01:47:43,707 --> 01:47:46,870
Who shall call them
from the grey twilight?

1138
01:47:47,336 --> 01:47:49,543
The forgotten people.

1139
01:47:49,713 --> 01:47:52,204
The heir of him to whom
the oath they swore.

1140
01:47:52,716 --> 01:47:54,581
From the north shall he come.

1141
01:47:55,094 --> 01:47:56,709
Need shall drive him.

1142
01:47:57,846 --> 01:48:01,338
He shall pass the door
to the Paths of the Dead.

1143
01:48:19,827 --> 01:48:23,115
The very warmth of my blood
seems stolen away.

1144
01:48:28,669 --> 01:48:30,625
The way is shut.

1145
01:48:31,380 --> 01:48:33,336
It was made by those
who are dead.

1146
01:48:33,924 --> 01:48:36,210
And the Dead keep it.

1147
01:48:36,760 --> 01:48:38,250
The way is shut.

1148
01:48:38,595 --> 01:48:41,211
[LOUD EXHALATION]

1149
01:48:42,599 --> 01:48:44,555
[HORSES WHINNYING]

1150
01:48:49,648 --> 01:48:51,138
Brego!

1151
01:48:54,653 --> 01:48:57,360
I do not fear death.

1152
01:49:09,668 --> 01:49:12,080
Well, this is a thing unheard-of.

1153
01:49:12,254 --> 01:49:16,918
An Elf will go underground
where a Dwarf dare not?

1154
01:49:17,092 --> 01:49:18,423
Oh.

1155
01:49:18,594 --> 01:49:21,427
Oh, I'd never hear the end of it.

1156
01:49:36,445 --> 01:49:38,652
We must ride light and swift.

1157
01:49:38,822 --> 01:49:40,608
It is a long road ahead.

1158
01:49:40,783 --> 01:49:43,820
And man and beast must reach the end
with the strength to fight.

1159
01:49:49,333 --> 01:49:52,325
Little Hobbits do not belong in war,
Master Meriadoc.

1160
01:49:52,711 --> 01:49:54,667
All my friends have gone to battle.

1161
01:49:54,838 --> 01:49:56,749
I would be ashamed to be left behind.

1162
01:49:56,924 --> 01:49:59,006
It is a three-day gallop to Minas Tirith.

1163
01:49:59,218 --> 01:50:01,584
And none of my riders can bear you
as a burden.

1164
01:50:02,596 --> 01:50:04,712
I want to fight.

1165
01:50:05,224 --> 01:50:07,215
I will say no more.

1166
01:50:19,488 --> 01:50:21,194
[GASPS]

1167
01:50:24,034 --> 01:50:25,990
Ride with me.

1168
01:50:27,454 --> 01:50:28,864
My lady.

1169
01:50:29,039 --> 01:50:31,371
ÉOMER:
Form up! Move out!

1170
01:50:31,542 --> 01:50:34,784
Form up! Move out!

1171
01:50:37,881 --> 01:50:39,041
THÉODEN:
Ride!

1172
01:50:39,258 --> 01:50:42,216
Ride now to Gondor!

1173
01:50:54,398 --> 01:50:57,561
[ORCS CHANTING]

1174
01:51:23,844 --> 01:51:25,584
GIMLI:
What is it?

1175
01:51:25,762 --> 01:51:27,298
What do you see?

1176
01:51:27,556 --> 01:51:29,672
I see shapes of men.

1177
01:51:32,352 --> 01:51:33,717
And of horses.

1178
01:51:34,438 --> 01:51:35,678
Where?

1179
01:51:35,856 --> 01:51:38,814
LEGOLAS:
Pale banners like shreds of cloud.

1180
01:51:41,236 --> 01:51:43,443
Spears rise...

1181
01:51:44,072 --> 01:51:47,530
...like winter-thickets
through a shroud of mist.

1182
01:51:48,785 --> 01:51:50,946
The Dead are following.

1183
01:51:52,122 --> 01:51:53,612
They have been summoned.

1184
01:51:54,333 --> 01:51:56,119
The Dead?

1185
01:51:56,543 --> 01:51:58,249
Summoned?

1186
01:51:58,629 --> 01:52:00,540
I knew that.

1187
01:52:01,089 --> 01:52:03,250
Huh. Ha.

1188
01:52:03,884 --> 01:52:05,624
Very good.

1189
01:52:06,345 --> 01:52:08,427
Very good! Legolas!

1190
01:52:20,317 --> 01:52:22,433
[BLOWING]

1191
01:52:46,385 --> 01:52:47,795
Do not look down.

1192
01:52:54,309 --> 01:52:55,799
[CRACKS]

1193
01:53:01,358 --> 01:53:03,519
[BONES CRACKING]

1194
01:53:18,333 --> 01:53:20,119
[PANTING]

1195
01:53:40,397 --> 01:53:45,517
KING OF THE DEAD:
<i>Who enters my domain?</i>

1196
01:53:49,239 --> 01:53:51,480
One who will have your allegiance.

1197
01:53:54,453 --> 01:53:59,743
The Dead do not suffer the living to pass.

1198
01:54:00,083 --> 01:54:02,745
You will suffer me.

1199
01:54:02,961 --> 01:54:05,498
[CACKLING]

1200
01:54:26,276 --> 01:54:29,689
KING OF THE DEAD:
The way is shut.

1201
01:54:30,864 --> 01:54:35,278
It was made by those who are dead.

1202
01:54:35,702 --> 01:54:39,866
And the Dead keep it.

1203
01:54:49,007 --> 01:54:52,090
The way is shut.

1204
01:54:53,804 --> 01:54:56,466
Now you must die.

1205
01:55:00,310 --> 01:55:03,143
I summon you to fulfill your oath.

1206
01:55:03,522 --> 01:55:08,482
None but the king of Gondor
may command me.

1207
01:55:09,945 --> 01:55:11,936
[YELLS]

1208
01:55:14,074 --> 01:55:16,235
That line was broken.

1209
01:55:17,160 --> 01:55:18,650
[GROANS]

1210
01:55:18,829 --> 01:55:21,070
It has been remade.

1211
01:55:29,005 --> 01:55:30,495
Fight for us...

1212
01:55:30,674 --> 01:55:33,256
...and regain your honor.

1213
01:55:37,431 --> 01:55:38,762
What say you?

1214
01:55:50,986 --> 01:55:52,522
What say you?

1215
01:55:52,696 --> 01:55:55,028
Ah! You waste your time, Aragorn.

1216
01:55:55,198 --> 01:55:58,361
They had no honor in life,
they have none now in death.

1217
01:55:58,869 --> 01:56:01,360
I am Isildur's heir.

1218
01:56:01,955 --> 01:56:03,866
Fight for me...

1219
01:56:04,499 --> 01:56:08,083
...and I will hold your oaths fulfilled.

1220
01:56:12,007 --> 01:56:13,963
What say you?

1221
01:56:15,218 --> 01:56:18,381
[CACKLING]

1222
01:56:21,892 --> 01:56:24,099
You have my word!

1223
01:56:24,394 --> 01:56:28,387
Fight, and I will release you
from this living death!

1224
01:56:29,858 --> 01:56:31,348
What say you?!

1225
01:56:34,654 --> 01:56:37,612
Stand, you traitors!

1226
01:56:44,706 --> 01:56:46,412
[CRACKING]

1227
01:56:47,250 --> 01:56:48,990
[RUMBLING]

1228
01:57:04,559 --> 01:57:05,594
Out!

1229
01:57:26,957 --> 01:57:28,538
Legolas!

1230
01:57:29,668 --> 01:57:30,874
Run!

1231
01:58:25,348 --> 01:58:27,839
[WIND WHISTLING]

1232
01:58:37,193 --> 01:58:39,229
We fight.

1233
01:58:42,532 --> 01:58:45,023
[ORCS YELLING AND
TROLLS GRUNTING]

1234
01:58:49,623 --> 01:58:52,205
IORLAS:
Open the gate! Quick!

1235
01:59:17,275 --> 01:59:19,140
[GROWLS]

1236
01:59:23,239 --> 01:59:25,230
Quick! Hurry!

1237
01:59:39,005 --> 01:59:40,586
Faramir!

1238
01:59:41,591 --> 01:59:44,879
Say not that he has fallen.

1239
01:59:46,054 --> 01:59:47,590
They were outnumbered.

1240
01:59:48,014 --> 01:59:49,595
None survived.

1241
01:59:50,308 --> 01:59:52,299
Fear.

1242
01:59:52,852 --> 01:59:56,060
The city is rank with it.

1243
01:59:58,400 --> 02:00:00,857
Let us ease their pain.

1244
02:00:01,111 --> 02:00:02,851
Release the prisoners.

1245
02:00:03,029 --> 02:00:04,940
Catapults!

1246
02:00:05,198 --> 02:00:07,189
[ORCS YELLING]

1247
02:00:08,243 --> 02:00:10,325
MAN:
Shields up!

1248
02:00:18,336 --> 02:00:21,794
DENETHOR:
My sons are spent.

1249
02:00:22,841 --> 02:00:25,753
My line has ended.

1250
02:00:28,596 --> 02:00:29,961
PIPPIN:
He's alive!

1251
02:00:30,140 --> 02:00:33,303
The House of Stewards has failed.

1252
02:00:33,476 --> 02:00:34,966
He needs medicine, my lord.

1253
02:00:35,979 --> 02:00:38,641
My line has ended!

1254
02:00:40,150 --> 02:00:42,141
PIPPIN:
My lord!

1255
02:00:49,159 --> 02:00:51,241
ORC:
Put it in!

1256
02:00:55,665 --> 02:00:57,496
Rohan...

1257
02:00:58,293 --> 02:01:00,659
...has deserted us.

1258
02:01:05,759 --> 02:01:07,670
[PEOPLE SCREAMING]

1259
02:01:07,886 --> 02:01:09,001
[CHUCKLES]

1260
02:01:09,304 --> 02:01:12,171
[BOULDERS CRASHING,
PEOPLE SCREAMING]

1261
02:01:15,143 --> 02:01:18,351
Théoden's betrayed me.

1262
02:01:29,491 --> 02:01:31,322
Abandon your posts!

1263
02:01:32,368 --> 02:01:36,281
Flee! Flee for your lives!

1264
02:01:38,792 --> 02:01:40,623
Oh!

1265
02:01:41,711 --> 02:01:43,292
[GRUNTS]

1266
02:01:46,424 --> 02:01:47,960
Prepare for battle!

1267
02:01:48,510 --> 02:01:51,673
Hurry, men! To the wall! Defend the wall!

1268
02:01:52,847 --> 02:01:54,803
MAN:
Over here!

1269
02:01:55,558 --> 02:01:57,924
GANDALF:
Return to your posts!

1270
02:02:08,738 --> 02:02:11,354
Send these foul beasts into the abyss.

1271
02:02:21,543 --> 02:02:22,999
Stay where you are.

1272
02:02:39,978 --> 02:02:41,388
SOLDIER 1:
We need more rubble!

1273
02:02:41,563 --> 02:02:43,428
SOLDIER 2:
Watch out!

1274
02:02:43,606 --> 02:02:46,097
SOLDIER 3:
Down to the lower levels. Quick!

1275
02:02:48,027 --> 02:02:49,563
SOLDIER 4:
Double up, men!

1276
02:03:05,628 --> 02:03:07,084
Yah!

1277
02:03:08,131 --> 02:03:09,621
[SQUEALS, GROANS]

1278
02:03:09,883 --> 02:03:11,248
[SPITS]

1279
02:03:11,467 --> 02:03:13,958
[RINGWRAITHS SCREECHING]

1280
02:03:47,921 --> 02:03:49,786
[SCREAMS]

1281
02:03:58,556 --> 02:04:01,548
Hold them back! Do not give in to fear.

1282
02:04:02,060 --> 02:04:05,552
Stand to your posts! Fight!

1283
02:04:11,569 --> 02:04:13,651
[SOLDIERS SCREAMING]

1284
02:04:46,229 --> 02:04:47,844
Not at the towers!

1285
02:04:48,022 --> 02:04:51,014
Aim for the trolls! Kill the trolls!

1286
02:04:51,734 --> 02:04:53,599
Bring them down!

1287
02:05:28,730 --> 02:05:30,766
Fight them back!

1288
02:05:30,940 --> 02:05:32,931
Peregrin Took!

1289
02:05:33,776 --> 02:05:36,939
-Go back to the Citadel!
-They'd called us out to fight.

1290
02:05:47,665 --> 02:05:49,280
[YELLS]

1291
02:05:52,670 --> 02:05:55,036
This is no place for a Hobbit.

1292
02:06:20,782 --> 02:06:22,238
Guard of the Citadel, indeed.

1293
02:06:22,825 --> 02:06:26,192
Now, back, up the hill. Quickly. Quick!

1294
02:06:37,507 --> 02:06:40,499
What are you doing,
you useless scum?!

1295
02:06:40,676 --> 02:06:42,632
The door won't give. It's too strong.

1296
02:06:48,976 --> 02:06:51,342
Get back there and smash it down.

1297
02:06:51,521 --> 02:06:53,512
But nothing can breach it.

1298
02:06:56,484 --> 02:06:58,725
Grond will breach it.

1299
02:07:02,156 --> 02:07:04,238
Bring up the wolf's head.

1300
02:07:07,370 --> 02:07:12,740
[ORCS CHANTING]
<i>Grond! Grond! Grond! Grond!</i>

1301
02:07:13,042 --> 02:07:16,876
<i>Grond! Grond! Grond!</i>

1302
02:07:18,840 --> 02:07:22,253
<i>Grond! Grond! Grond!</i>

1303
02:07:22,969 --> 02:07:26,632
<i>Grond! Grond! Grond!</i>

1304
02:07:27,056 --> 02:07:31,220
<i>Grond! Grond! Grond!</i>

1305
02:07:31,394 --> 02:07:35,012
<i>Grond! Grond! Grond!</i>

1306
02:07:46,409 --> 02:07:48,946
[CHATTERING INDISTINCTLY]

1307
02:07:56,252 --> 02:07:58,038
ARAGORN:
You may go no further.

1308
02:08:01,257 --> 02:08:03,418
You will not enter Gondor.

1309
02:08:03,509 --> 02:08:04,919
[SAILORS LAUGH]

1310
02:08:05,011 --> 02:08:06,967
Who are you to deny us passage?

1311
02:08:07,054 --> 02:08:10,888
Legolas, fire a warning shot
past the bosun's ear.

1312
02:08:13,102 --> 02:08:14,717
Mind your aim.

1313
02:08:18,107 --> 02:08:19,472
[YELLS]

1314
02:08:19,567 --> 02:08:21,353
Oh!

1315
02:08:21,444 --> 02:08:23,935
That's it. Right. We warned you.

1316
02:08:24,030 --> 02:08:25,770
Prepare to be boarded.

1317
02:08:25,865 --> 02:08:27,446
[SAILORS LAUGH]

1318
02:08:27,533 --> 02:08:28,943
CORSAIR BOSUN:
Boarded?

1319
02:08:29,035 --> 02:08:30,741
By you and whose army?

1320
02:08:32,288 --> 02:08:34,574
This army.

1321
02:08:34,957 --> 02:08:37,243
[YELLING]

1322
02:08:38,294 --> 02:08:40,250
[YELLING]

1323
02:08:51,265 --> 02:08:53,096
In there.

1324
02:08:54,769 --> 02:08:56,634
What is this place?

1325
02:08:57,146 --> 02:08:59,307
[WATER DRIPPING]

1326
02:09:01,025 --> 02:09:04,438
Master must go inside the tunnel.

1327
02:09:05,821 --> 02:09:09,814
Now that I'm here, I don't think I want to.

1328
02:09:11,911 --> 02:09:14,152
It's the only way.

1329
02:09:16,499 --> 02:09:18,490
Go in...

1330
02:09:19,043 --> 02:09:21,284
...or go back.

1331
02:09:23,965 --> 02:09:26,707
I can't go back.

1332
02:09:36,477 --> 02:09:38,138
[FRODO GRUNTS]

1333
02:09:38,938 --> 02:09:41,680
-What's that smell?
GOLLUM: Orcses' filth.

1334
02:09:41,774 --> 02:09:45,016
Orcses come in here sometimes.

1335
02:09:50,032 --> 02:09:51,863
Hurry.

1336
02:09:56,747 --> 02:09:58,703
This way.

1337
02:10:01,544 --> 02:10:03,375
Sméagol?

1338
02:10:04,338 --> 02:10:06,499
GOLLUM:
Over here.

1339
02:10:11,345 --> 02:10:12,710
Oh!

1340
02:10:12,805 --> 02:10:14,636
Aah! Aah!

1341
02:10:14,724 --> 02:10:17,966
It's sticky. What is it?

1342
02:10:18,060 --> 02:10:20,426
GOLLUM:
You'll see.

1343
02:10:20,521 --> 02:10:22,933
Oh, yes.

1344
02:10:23,024 --> 02:10:26,232
You will see.

1345
02:10:35,119 --> 02:10:36,780
Sméagol?

1346
02:10:38,080 --> 02:10:39,411
Sméagol!

1347
02:10:42,084 --> 02:10:44,040
Sméagol!

1348
02:10:53,262 --> 02:10:55,253
Sam.

1349
02:11:14,325 --> 02:11:16,532
[GROWLING]

1350
02:12:29,108 --> 02:12:31,190
[WHIMPERING]

1351
02:12:35,322 --> 02:12:37,483
GALADRIEL:
<i>And you, Frodo Baggins...</i>

1352
02:12:37,575 --> 02:12:42,990
<i>...I give you the light of Eärendil,</i>
<i>our most beloved star.</i>

1353
02:12:43,747 --> 02:12:47,080
<i>May it be a light for you</i>
<i>in dark places...</i>

1354
02:12:47,168 --> 02:12:50,752
<i>...when all other lights go out.</i>

1355
02:12:50,838 --> 02:12:53,204
[SPEAKING ELVISH]

1356
02:13:07,396 --> 02:13:09,057
[SCREECHES]

1357
02:13:16,405 --> 02:13:17,895
[SCREECHES]

1358
02:13:26,540 --> 02:13:28,155
[HISSING]

1359
02:14:07,122 --> 02:14:10,455
GOLLUM [SINGING]:
<i>Naughty little fly</i>

1360
02:14:10,543 --> 02:14:13,785
<i>Why does he cry?</i>

1361
02:14:14,296 --> 02:14:17,663
<i>Caught in a web</i>

1362
02:14:17,758 --> 02:14:20,591
<i>Soon you'll be....</i>

1363
02:14:20,970 --> 02:14:22,801
Eaten.

1364
02:14:23,973 --> 02:14:26,134
[GRUNTS, YELLS]

1365
02:14:59,967 --> 02:15:02,709
Got away, did it, precious?

1366
02:15:02,803 --> 02:15:05,010
Not this time.

1367
02:15:05,097 --> 02:15:08,180
-Not this time!
-No!

1368
02:15:11,395 --> 02:15:13,511
[SCREAMING]

1369
02:15:15,024 --> 02:15:18,357
It wasn't us. It wasn't us!

1370
02:15:18,861 --> 02:15:21,523
Sméagol wouldn't hurt master.

1371
02:15:21,614 --> 02:15:23,570
We promised.

1372
02:15:23,657 --> 02:15:26,239
You must believe us.

1373
02:15:26,327 --> 02:15:28,158
It was the precious.

1374
02:15:28,245 --> 02:15:33,035
The precious made us do it.

1375
02:15:37,671 --> 02:15:39,707
[GOLLUM SOBBING]

1376
02:15:50,184 --> 02:15:53,051
I have to destroy it, Sméagol.

1377
02:16:02,071 --> 02:16:05,404
I have to destroy it for both our sakes.

1378
02:16:15,584 --> 02:16:16,915
No!

1379
02:16:18,420 --> 02:16:20,536
[SCREAMS]

1380
02:16:21,715 --> 02:16:23,751
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

1381
02:16:40,150 --> 02:16:42,607
I'm so sorry, Sam.

1382
02:16:47,074 --> 02:16:49,611
I'm so sorry.

1383
02:17:15,394 --> 02:17:20,184
GALADRIEL: <i>This task was appointed</i>
<i>to you, Frodo of the Shire.</i>

1384
02:17:21,316 --> 02:17:23,773
<i>If you do not find a way...</i>

1385
02:17:24,987 --> 02:17:26,272
<i>...no one will.</i>

1386
02:18:00,063 --> 02:18:02,896
ÉOMER: The scouts report
Minas Tirith is surrounded.

1387
02:18:02,983 --> 02:18:05,315
The lower level's in flames.

1388
02:18:05,736 --> 02:18:08,227
Everywhere,
legions of the enemy advance.

1389
02:18:08,322 --> 02:18:09,562
Time is against us.

1390
02:18:10,199 --> 02:18:11,564
Make ready!

1391
02:18:11,658 --> 02:18:13,569
Take heart, Merry.

1392
02:18:13,660 --> 02:18:15,867
It will soon be over.

1393
02:18:16,497 --> 02:18:18,033
My lady...

1394
02:18:18,665 --> 02:18:21,202
...you are fair and brave...

1395
02:18:21,543 --> 02:18:24,000
...and have much to live for...

1396
02:18:25,339 --> 02:18:27,705
...and many who love you.

1397
02:18:30,511 --> 02:18:33,218
I know it is too late to turn aside.

1398
02:18:33,764 --> 02:18:37,006
I know there is not much point
now in hoping.

1399
02:18:38,227 --> 02:18:41,640
If I were a knight of Rohan,
capable of great deeds....

1400
02:18:41,730 --> 02:18:44,938
But I'm not.

1401
02:18:45,025 --> 02:18:46,890
I'm a Hobbit.

1402
02:18:49,613 --> 02:18:52,104
And I know I can't save Middle-earth.

1403
02:18:55,536 --> 02:18:57,868
I just want to help my friends.

1404
02:18:59,915 --> 02:19:01,405
Frodo.

1405
02:19:02,251 --> 02:19:04,037
Sam.

1406
02:19:05,587 --> 02:19:07,623
Pippin.

1407
02:19:09,091 --> 02:19:12,128
More than anything,
I wish I could see them again.

1408
02:19:16,390 --> 02:19:18,756
ÉOMER:
Prepare to move out!

1409
02:19:18,851 --> 02:19:21,638
Make haste.
We ride through the night.

1410
02:19:22,896 --> 02:19:25,308
[HORN BLOWING]

1411
02:19:38,287 --> 02:19:39,618
To battle.

1412
02:19:40,080 --> 02:19:41,490
To battle.

1413
02:20:04,605 --> 02:20:06,345
Back to the gate!

1414
02:20:06,648 --> 02:20:08,809
Hurry!

1415
02:20:28,712 --> 02:20:33,251
I am steward of the House of Anárion.

1416
02:20:33,342 --> 02:20:35,799
Thus have I walked.

1417
02:20:37,012 --> 02:20:40,095
And thus now will I sleep.

1418
02:20:46,146 --> 02:20:48,228
Gondor is lost.

1419
02:20:48,690 --> 02:20:52,182
There is no hope for Men.

1420
02:21:06,750 --> 02:21:09,617
Why do the fools fly?

1421
02:21:11,171 --> 02:21:14,208
Better to die sooner than late.

1422
02:21:16,385 --> 02:21:18,421
For die we must.

1423
02:21:30,565 --> 02:21:33,648
No tomb for Denethor
and Faramir.

1424
02:21:34,736 --> 02:21:40,777
No long, slow sleep of death embalmed.

1425
02:21:40,867 --> 02:21:46,078
We shall burn,
like the heathen kings of old.

1426
02:21:49,751 --> 02:21:51,537
Bring wood and oil.

1427
02:21:54,381 --> 02:21:55,791
GANDALF:
Steady.

1428
02:21:55,882 --> 02:21:57,964
Steady.

1429
02:22:12,399 --> 02:22:14,936
You are soldiers of Gondor.

1430
02:22:15,193 --> 02:22:19,607
No matter what comes through that gate,
you will stand your ground.

1431
02:22:22,826 --> 02:22:24,487
[ROARING]

1432
02:22:26,121 --> 02:22:27,281
SOLDIER:
Run!

1433
02:22:29,207 --> 02:22:30,697
Volley!

1434
02:22:31,460 --> 02:22:33,371
Fire!

1435
02:22:33,462 --> 02:22:35,703
[SHRIEKS]

1436
02:23:43,782 --> 02:23:45,864
[ROCKS FALLING]

1437
02:23:52,541 --> 02:23:54,657
[GRUNTING]

1438
02:24:26,449 --> 02:24:28,531
Let him go, you filth.

1439
02:24:28,827 --> 02:24:30,283
[SCREECHES]

1440
02:24:30,370 --> 02:24:32,076
Let him go!

1441
02:24:33,373 --> 02:24:35,534
You will not touch him again.

1442
02:24:38,628 --> 02:24:40,539
Come on and finish it.

1443
02:24:47,345 --> 02:24:48,755
[YELLS, GRUNTS]

1444
02:25:11,661 --> 02:25:13,117
[SHELOB SQUEALS]

1445
02:25:14,956 --> 02:25:16,412
[GRUNTS]

1446
02:26:12,514 --> 02:26:14,425
[SHELOB SQUEALING]

1447
02:26:29,531 --> 02:26:31,863
Ha! Back!

1448
02:26:42,711 --> 02:26:43,996
Mr. Frodo.

1449
02:26:53,555 --> 02:26:55,591
Oh, no.

1450
02:26:55,682 --> 02:26:57,673
Frodo.

1451
02:26:57,976 --> 02:26:59,841
Mr. Frodo.

1452
02:27:04,399 --> 02:27:05,730
Wake up.

1453
02:27:09,571 --> 02:27:11,983
Don't leave me here alone.

1454
02:27:13,491 --> 02:27:15,903
Don't go where I can't follow.

1455
02:27:20,248 --> 02:27:21,579
Wake up.

1456
02:27:28,256 --> 02:27:30,497
Not asleep.

1457
02:27:32,594 --> 02:27:34,550
Dead.

1458
02:27:51,154 --> 02:27:53,145
[ORCS GROWLING]

1459
02:27:53,239 --> 02:27:54,775
SHAGRAT:
You get back, you scum!

1460
02:28:04,417 --> 02:28:05,748
GORBAG:
What's this?

1461
02:28:06,920 --> 02:28:09,627
Looks like old Shelob's
been having a bit of fun.

1462
02:28:11,633 --> 02:28:14,215
SHAGRAT:
Killed another one, has she?

1463
02:28:14,302 --> 02:28:16,293
No.

1464
02:28:19,057 --> 02:28:21,048
This fellow ain't dead.

1465
02:28:21,351 --> 02:28:23,683
[WHISPERING]
Not dead?

1466
02:28:23,770 --> 02:28:29,640
She jabs him with her stinger,
and he goes as limp as a boned fish.

1467
02:28:29,984 --> 02:28:32,691
Then she has her way with them.

1468
02:28:33,071 --> 02:28:34,777
That's how she likes to feed.

1469
02:28:35,281 --> 02:28:37,442
Fresh blood.

1470
02:28:37,534 --> 02:28:39,866
Get him to the tower!

1471
02:28:43,331 --> 02:28:45,071
Samwise, you fool.

1472
02:28:45,166 --> 02:28:48,078
TOWER ORC: This scum will be awake
in a couple of hours.

1473
02:28:48,169 --> 02:28:50,706
Then he'll wish he'd never been born.

1474
02:29:03,643 --> 02:29:05,099
[WHIMPERS FAINTLY]

1475
02:29:05,520 --> 02:29:07,636
[BATTLE SOUNDS IN DISTANCE]

1476
02:29:15,029 --> 02:29:18,237
The house of his spirit crumbles.

1477
02:29:19,325 --> 02:29:20,735
He is burning.

1478
02:29:21,870 --> 02:29:23,201
Already burning.

1479
02:29:23,621 --> 02:29:25,612
PIPPIN:
He's not dead.

1480
02:29:26,040 --> 02:29:27,701
He's not dead!

1481
02:29:29,919 --> 02:29:31,750
No! No!

1482
02:29:31,838 --> 02:29:34,250
No! No!

1483
02:29:34,340 --> 02:29:36,376
He's not dead!

1484
02:29:36,759 --> 02:29:40,251
-Farewell, Peregrin, son of Paladin.
PIPPIN: No! No! No!

1485
02:29:40,346 --> 02:29:43,713
I release you from my service.

1486
02:29:45,059 --> 02:29:49,393
Go now and die in what way
seems best to you.

1487
02:29:51,566 --> 02:29:53,898
Pour oil on the wood!

1488
02:29:55,653 --> 02:29:57,689
SOLDIER:
Come on, soldier! Move it!

1489
02:29:58,198 --> 02:30:01,065
-Hurry along there! Hurry along!
-Gandalf!

1490
02:30:01,451 --> 02:30:02,907
Where is Gandalf?

1491
02:30:04,078 --> 02:30:05,318
Gandalf!

1492
02:30:10,752 --> 02:30:11,912
GANDALF:
Retreat!

1493
02:30:14,088 --> 02:30:15,919
The city is breached!

1494
02:30:16,007 --> 02:30:18,965
Fall back to the second level!

1495
02:30:22,764 --> 02:30:24,379
Get the women and children out!

1496
02:30:24,766 --> 02:30:26,552
Get them out!

1497
02:30:26,643 --> 02:30:28,179
Retreat!

1498
02:30:28,269 --> 02:30:30,100
SOLDIER:
Come on. Come on.

1499
02:30:30,438 --> 02:30:34,727
Move into the city. Kill all in your path.

1500
02:30:35,109 --> 02:30:37,191
[ORCS YELLING INDISTINCTLY]

1501
02:30:42,742 --> 02:30:45,108
GUARD:
Take them down!

1502
02:30:47,205 --> 02:30:49,287
[WOMEN SCREAMING]

1503
02:31:05,640 --> 02:31:08,598
GANDALF:
Fight. Fight to the last man!

1504
02:31:08,685 --> 02:31:10,016
Fight for your lives!

1505
02:31:10,103 --> 02:31:11,434
Gandalf!

1506
02:31:15,817 --> 02:31:17,182
Gandalf!

1507
02:31:17,277 --> 02:31:19,984
Denethor has lost his mind!

1508
02:31:20,071 --> 02:31:22,403
He's burning Faramir alive!

1509
02:31:22,490 --> 02:31:24,321
Up! Quickly!

1510
02:31:27,996 --> 02:31:29,452
[ROARING]

1511
02:31:31,165 --> 02:31:32,655
Go back to the abyss.

1512
02:31:34,168 --> 02:31:37,376
Fall into the nothingness
that awaits you and your master.

1513
02:31:37,463 --> 02:31:44,050
WITCH-KING: Do you not know death
when you see it, old man?

1514
02:31:44,137 --> 02:31:48,927
This is my hour.

1515
02:31:49,017 --> 02:31:51,258
[WITCH-KING SCREECHING]

1516
02:31:58,401 --> 02:32:00,016
Gandalf!

1517
02:32:02,030 --> 02:32:03,361
[YELLS]

1518
02:32:08,870 --> 02:32:12,408
WITCH-KING:
You have failed.

1519
02:32:13,207 --> 02:32:18,042
The world of Men will fall.

1520
02:32:23,217 --> 02:32:25,378
[HORN BLOWING]

1521
02:33:03,966 --> 02:33:06,457
[ORCS CHANTING]

1522
02:33:15,353 --> 02:33:16,809
Courage, Merry.

1523
02:33:16,896 --> 02:33:19,353
Courage for our friends.

1524
02:33:22,902 --> 02:33:25,985
GOTHMOG:
Form ranks, you maggots. Form ranks!

1525
02:33:26,072 --> 02:33:29,405
Pikes in front. Archers behind.

1526
02:33:37,458 --> 02:33:40,666
THÉODEN: Éomer, take your éored
down the left flank.

1527
02:33:40,753 --> 02:33:42,118
ÉOMER:
Flank ready.

1528
02:33:42,213 --> 02:33:45,171
THÉODEN: Gamling, follow the king's
banner down the center.

1529
02:33:45,258 --> 02:33:49,001
Grimbold, take your company right
after you pass the wall.

1530
02:33:49,095 --> 02:33:51,962
Forth, and fear no darkness!

1531
02:33:52,056 --> 02:33:56,015
Arise, arise, Riders of Théoden!

1532
02:33:56,102 --> 02:34:01,392
Spears shall be shaken,
shields shall be splintered...

1533
02:34:01,482 --> 02:34:05,316
...a sword-day, a red day...

1534
02:34:05,403 --> 02:34:08,987
...ere the sun rises!

1535
02:34:16,789 --> 02:34:21,123
Whatever happens, stay with me.
I'll look after you.

1536
02:34:23,796 --> 02:34:25,957
[CLANGING]

1537
02:34:27,467 --> 02:34:29,503
THÉODEN:
Ride now!

1538
02:34:30,970 --> 02:34:33,131
Ride now!

1539
02:34:33,681 --> 02:34:36,514
Ride! Ride for ruin...

1540
02:34:36,601 --> 02:34:39,434
...and the world's ending!

1541
02:34:41,314 --> 02:34:42,770
Death!

1542
02:34:43,149 --> 02:34:46,141
ALL:
Death!

1543
02:34:46,235 --> 02:34:49,477
THÉODEN: Death!
ALL: Death!

1544
02:34:49,947 --> 02:34:51,483
THÉODEN: Death!
ALL: Death!

1545
02:34:52,200 --> 02:34:55,658
-Death!
-Death!

1546
02:35:00,792 --> 02:35:03,158
Forth Eorlingas!

1547
02:35:03,628 --> 02:35:06,495
[HORNS SOUNDING]

1548
02:35:10,426 --> 02:35:12,166
[RIDERS YELLING]

1549
02:35:46,170 --> 02:35:47,876
Fire!

1550
02:35:51,717 --> 02:35:52,877
Death!

1551
02:35:57,098 --> 02:35:58,383
Charge!

1552
02:35:58,891 --> 02:36:00,472
Fire at will!

1553
02:36:08,526 --> 02:36:10,562
[YELLS]

1554
02:36:25,918 --> 02:36:27,249
[YELLS]

1555
02:36:37,805 --> 02:36:39,215
[YELLS]

1556
02:36:48,316 --> 02:36:50,523
[BREATHING UNEVENLY]

1557
02:36:57,783 --> 02:37:01,116
Set a fire in our flesh.

1558
02:37:18,763 --> 02:37:20,469
Stay this madness!

1559
02:37:24,810 --> 02:37:29,429
You may triumph in the field of battle
for a day...

1560
02:37:29,982 --> 02:37:33,645
...but against the power that has risen
in the east...

1561
02:37:33,736 --> 02:37:36,978
...there is no victory.

1562
02:37:58,010 --> 02:37:59,671
[YELLS]

1563
02:38:06,185 --> 02:38:08,016
No!

1564
02:38:08,104 --> 02:38:10,846
You will not take my son from me!

1565
02:38:10,940 --> 02:38:13,397
No! No!

1566
02:38:13,484 --> 02:38:14,849
Yah!

1567
02:38:15,903 --> 02:38:17,518
[YELLS]

1568
02:38:24,203 --> 02:38:25,864
Faramir.

1569
02:38:30,543 --> 02:38:33,034
[SCREAMING]

1570
02:38:39,427 --> 02:38:43,386
So passes Denethor, son of Ecthelion.

1571
02:39:10,916 --> 02:39:12,747
Drive them to the river!

1572
02:39:15,463 --> 02:39:17,454
Make safe the city!

1573
02:39:19,216 --> 02:39:21,127
[OLIPHAUNTS ROARING]

1574
02:39:21,218 --> 02:39:23,425
[FOOTSTEPS THUDDING]

1575
02:39:33,898 --> 02:39:36,605
[HORN BLOWING]

1576
02:39:39,737 --> 02:39:41,898
[HARADRIM CHANTING]

1577
02:39:57,463 --> 02:39:59,454
Re-form the line!

1578
02:40:00,591 --> 02:40:02,502
Re-form the line!

1579
02:40:09,517 --> 02:40:12,133
Sound the charge! Take them head-on!

1580
02:40:12,812 --> 02:40:14,973
Charge!

1581
02:40:17,233 --> 02:40:18,848
[YELLS]

1582
02:41:11,203 --> 02:41:12,864
[YELLS]

1583
02:41:33,893 --> 02:41:35,303
MAN 1:
Cut him down!

1584
02:41:37,062 --> 02:41:39,018
MAN 2:
Follow me!

1585
02:42:01,962 --> 02:42:04,578
Take the reins. Pull him left!

1586
02:42:06,967 --> 02:42:08,252
Left!

1587
02:42:25,653 --> 02:42:27,359
Aim for their heads!

1588
02:42:33,369 --> 02:42:36,611
Bring it down! Bring it down!
Bring it down!

1589
02:42:50,469 --> 02:42:51,959
Merry!

1590
02:43:13,325 --> 02:43:14,986
[COUGHS]

1591
02:43:40,144 --> 02:43:41,725
[GROWLS]

1592
02:43:51,363 --> 02:43:53,479
[FELL BEAST ROARS]

1593
02:43:59,163 --> 02:44:01,199
[POUNDING]

1594
02:44:05,377 --> 02:44:07,459
I didn't think it would end this way.

1595
02:44:08,714 --> 02:44:10,170
End?

1596
02:44:11,383 --> 02:44:13,544
No, the journey doesn't end here.

1597
02:44:16,055 --> 02:44:19,172
Death is just another path...

1598
02:44:19,725 --> 02:44:21,386
...one that we all must take.

1599
02:44:22,686 --> 02:44:26,144
The grey rain curtain
of this world rolls back...

1600
02:44:26,231 --> 02:44:29,894
...and all turns to silver glass.

1601
02:44:32,071 --> 02:44:34,062
And then you see it.

1602
02:44:35,991 --> 02:44:38,357
What, Gandalf?

1603
02:44:39,495 --> 02:44:40,780
See what?

1604
02:44:42,081 --> 02:44:44,242
White shores...

1605
02:44:45,918 --> 02:44:48,375
...and beyond.

1606
02:44:49,797 --> 02:44:51,583
A far green country...

1607
02:44:52,299 --> 02:44:55,257
...under a swift sunrise.

1608
02:44:59,264 --> 02:45:00,800
Well...

1609
02:45:00,891 --> 02:45:02,631
...that isn't so bad.

1610
02:45:02,726 --> 02:45:04,216
No.

1611
02:45:06,271 --> 02:45:07,932
No, it isn't.

1612
02:45:10,150 --> 02:45:12,266
[POUNDING CONTINUES,
TROLL GRUNTS]

1613
02:45:24,289 --> 02:45:27,656
Rally to me! To me!

1614
02:45:27,751 --> 02:45:30,743
[SCREECHES]

1615
02:45:33,132 --> 02:45:35,168
[ROARING]

1616
02:45:48,439 --> 02:45:52,978
WITCH-KING:
Feast on his flesh.

1617
02:45:57,322 --> 02:45:59,688
I will kill you if you touch him.

1618
02:45:59,783 --> 02:46:05,323
WITCH-KING: Do not come between
the Nazgûl and his prey.

1619
02:46:25,601 --> 02:46:28,308
[HISSES]

1620
02:46:39,907 --> 02:46:41,613
[SCREECHING]

1621
02:47:00,177 --> 02:47:01,883
[HISSES]

1622
02:47:13,732 --> 02:47:16,895
ORC COMMANDER:
Late as usual, pirate scum!

1623
02:47:17,361 --> 02:47:19,602
There's knife-work here needs doing.

1624
02:47:19,696 --> 02:47:22,938
Come on, you sea rats!
Get off your ships!

1625
02:47:38,423 --> 02:47:40,630
There's plenty for the both of us.

1626
02:47:40,717 --> 02:47:42,799
May the best Dwarf win.

1627
02:47:46,056 --> 02:47:48,092
[YELLS]

1628
02:48:00,279 --> 02:48:02,565
WITCH-KING:
You fool.

1629
02:48:02,656 --> 02:48:06,114
No man can kill me.

1630
02:48:08,453 --> 02:48:11,616
Die now.

1631
02:48:13,458 --> 02:48:14,948
[SCREECHES]

1632
02:48:15,043 --> 02:48:17,204
[SCREAMS]

1633
02:48:22,301 --> 02:48:24,337
I am no man.

1634
02:48:24,428 --> 02:48:26,134
[YELLS]

1635
02:48:40,861 --> 02:48:44,353
-Fifteen! Sixteen!
GIMLI: Seventeen!

1636
02:48:52,164 --> 02:48:54,029
Merry!

1637
02:48:54,791 --> 02:48:56,873
[YELLING]

1638
02:49:36,041 --> 02:49:37,872
Legolas!

1639
02:50:00,232 --> 02:50:02,598
Thirty-three, thirty-four.

1640
02:50:40,397 --> 02:50:42,433
[ROARS]

1641
02:50:49,740 --> 02:50:52,152
That still only counts as one!

1642
02:50:52,242 --> 02:50:54,449
Come on, then. Come on!

1643
02:51:38,163 --> 02:51:40,996
THÉODEN:
I know your face...

1644
02:51:42,834 --> 02:51:44,665
...Éowyn.

1645
02:51:47,297 --> 02:51:49,663
My eyes darken.

1646
02:51:50,801 --> 02:51:52,166
No.

1647
02:51:53,011 --> 02:51:54,626
No.

1648
02:51:56,681 --> 02:51:59,172
I am going to save you.

1649
02:52:00,519 --> 02:52:02,851
You already did.

1650
02:52:06,525 --> 02:52:08,186
Éowyn...

1651
02:52:09,694 --> 02:52:12,185
...my body is broken.

1652
02:52:17,202 --> 02:52:19,693
You have to let me go.

1653
02:52:22,374 --> 02:52:24,490
[MOUTHING]

1654
02:52:25,544 --> 02:52:28,160
I go to my fathers...

1655
02:52:29,589 --> 02:52:32,456
...in whose mighty company...

1656
02:52:32,884 --> 02:52:36,217
...I shall not now feel ashamed.

1657
02:52:52,863 --> 02:52:54,478
Éowyn.

1658
02:53:12,424 --> 02:53:14,540
[SOBBING]

1659
02:53:40,952 --> 02:53:43,443
Release us.

1660
02:53:45,332 --> 02:53:47,118
Bad idea.

1661
02:53:47,208 --> 02:53:51,121
Very handy in a tight spot, these lads,
despite the fact they're dead.

1662
02:53:51,212 --> 02:53:53,248
You gave us your word.

1663
02:53:54,966 --> 02:53:57,127
I hold your oath fulfilled.

1664
02:53:58,470 --> 02:53:59,801
Go.

1665
02:54:00,639 --> 02:54:02,300
Be at peace.

1666
02:54:02,682 --> 02:54:04,798
[SIGHS]

1667
02:54:05,810 --> 02:54:07,926
[WIND WHISTLING]

1668
02:54:08,313 --> 02:54:09,803
[GRUNTS]

1669
02:54:45,684 --> 02:54:47,595
Merry.

1670
02:54:48,186 --> 02:54:51,349
No!

1671
02:54:55,318 --> 02:54:57,684
No!

1672
02:56:44,803 --> 02:56:46,009
PIPPIN:
Merry!

1673
02:56:47,639 --> 02:56:49,630
Merry!

1674
02:57:00,985 --> 02:57:02,816
Merry.

1675
02:57:05,323 --> 02:57:06,529
Merry, it's me.

1676
02:57:09,160 --> 02:57:10,741
It's Pippin.

1677
02:57:13,248 --> 02:57:15,534
I knew you'd find me.

1678
02:57:15,625 --> 02:57:16,865
PIPPIN:
Yes.

1679
02:57:19,337 --> 02:57:21,373
Are you going to leave me?

1680
02:57:21,965 --> 02:57:23,671
No, Merry.

1681
02:57:24,968 --> 02:57:27,175
I'm going to look after you.

1682
02:57:49,367 --> 02:57:51,699
[ORCS GROWLING AND YELLING
IN DISTANCE]

1683
02:58:09,554 --> 02:58:11,090
[SNARLS]

1684
02:58:11,181 --> 02:58:12,671
Hands off!

1685
02:58:12,765 --> 02:58:15,928
That shiny shirt, that's mine.

1686
02:58:16,227 --> 02:58:20,391
It's going to the Great Eye,
along with everything else.

1687
02:58:21,900 --> 02:58:25,734
SHAGRAT: I don't take orders from
stinking Morgul-rats!

1688
02:58:26,571 --> 02:58:31,816
GORBAG: You touch it, and I'll stick
this blade in your gut.

1689
02:58:31,910 --> 02:58:33,366
[YELLING]

1690
02:58:52,430 --> 02:58:54,295
The scum tried to knife me.

1691
02:58:54,390 --> 02:58:56,130
Kill him!

1692
02:59:21,501 --> 02:59:23,412
[ROARS]

1693
02:59:35,139 --> 02:59:37,175
[FIGHTING IN DISTANCE]

1694
03:00:23,646 --> 03:00:25,307
[GRUNTING]

1695
03:00:36,576 --> 03:00:38,237
[SNARLS]

1696
03:00:39,370 --> 03:00:41,361
That's for Frodo!

1697
03:00:41,748 --> 03:00:43,864
And for the Shire!

1698
03:00:47,503 --> 03:00:49,585
And that's for my old Gaffer!

1699
03:01:13,363 --> 03:01:15,399
[GRUNTING]

1700
03:01:19,077 --> 03:01:22,410
Stop your squealing, you dunghill rat.

1701
03:01:23,581 --> 03:01:28,245
I'm gonna bleed you like a stuck pig.

1702
03:01:28,503 --> 03:01:30,585
[GASPS, DROPS SWORD]

1703
03:01:35,593 --> 03:01:38,300
-Not if I stick you first.
-Sam!

1704
03:01:38,388 --> 03:01:40,299
[GRUNTS, REMOVES SWORD]

1705
03:01:44,060 --> 03:01:46,142
Oh, Sam, I'm so sorry.

1706
03:01:46,229 --> 03:01:48,265
Sorry for everything.

1707
03:01:48,773 --> 03:01:52,482
SAM: Let's get you out of here.
-It's too late. It's over.

1708
03:01:52,568 --> 03:01:55,526
They've taken it. Sam...

1709
03:01:56,280 --> 03:01:57,770
...they took the Ring.

1710
03:01:58,574 --> 03:02:01,281
Begging your pardon, but they haven't.

1711
03:02:13,256 --> 03:02:15,463
I thought I'd lost you.

1712
03:02:15,800 --> 03:02:17,540
So I took it.

1713
03:02:18,678 --> 03:02:20,794
Only for safekeeping.

1714
03:02:22,056 --> 03:02:23,796
Give it to me.

1715
03:02:27,311 --> 03:02:29,552
Give me the Ring, Sam.

1716
03:02:31,065 --> 03:02:32,930
[VOICE OF THE RING WHISPERING]

1717
03:02:34,193 --> 03:02:35,478
[VOICE ECHOING]
Sam.

1718
03:02:37,071 --> 03:02:38,982
Give me the Ring.

1719
03:02:45,705 --> 03:02:47,161
[WHISPERING STOPS]

1720
03:02:59,719 --> 03:03:01,710
[IN NORMAL VOICE]
You must understand.

1721
03:03:04,515 --> 03:03:06,346
The Ring is my burden.

1722
03:03:07,518 --> 03:03:09,679
It will destroy you, Sam.

1723
03:03:09,979 --> 03:03:12,015
[BREATHING WITH DIFFICULTY]

1724
03:03:12,857 --> 03:03:14,848
Come on, Mr. Frodo.

1725
03:03:16,194 --> 03:03:17,855
We best find you some clothes.

1726
03:03:17,945 --> 03:03:21,028
You can't go walking through Mordor
in naught but your skin.

1727
03:03:42,720 --> 03:03:44,927
SAM:
We did it, Mr. Frodo.

1728
03:03:45,431 --> 03:03:47,717
We made it to Mordor.

1729
03:03:49,060 --> 03:03:50,721
FRODO:
There are so many of them.

1730
03:03:51,729 --> 03:03:54,266
We'll never get through unseen.

1731
03:03:59,403 --> 03:04:02,736
It's him, the Eye.

1732
03:04:10,456 --> 03:04:13,072
We have to go in there, Mr. Frodo.

1733
03:04:13,584 --> 03:04:15,575
There's nothing for it.

1734
03:04:18,589 --> 03:04:23,049
Come on. Let's just make it
down the hill for starters.

1735
03:04:32,395 --> 03:04:35,603
Frodo has passed beyond my sight.

1736
03:04:36,941 --> 03:04:39,808
The darkness is deepening.

1737
03:04:39,902 --> 03:04:42,359
If Sauron had the Ring,
we would know it.

1738
03:04:42,446 --> 03:04:44,562
It's only a matter of time.

1739
03:04:46,075 --> 03:04:48,441
He has suffered a defeat, yes...

1740
03:04:49,495 --> 03:04:54,080
...but behind the walls of Mordor,
our enemy is regrouping.

1741
03:04:54,166 --> 03:04:56,077
Let him stay there.

1742
03:04:56,168 --> 03:04:58,875
Let him rot! Why should we care?

1743
03:04:58,963 --> 03:05:04,208
Because 10,000 Orcs now stand
between Frodo and Mount Doom.

1744
03:05:10,975 --> 03:05:13,717
I've sent him to his death.

1745
03:05:15,229 --> 03:05:16,264
No.

1746
03:05:17,523 --> 03:05:19,229
There is still hope for Frodo.

1747
03:05:19,525 --> 03:05:23,643
He needs time and safe passage
across the plains of Gorgoroth.

1748
03:05:24,780 --> 03:05:27,317
-We can give him that.
-How?

1749
03:05:27,658 --> 03:05:30,400
Draw out Sauron's armies.

1750
03:05:30,494 --> 03:05:32,735
Empty his lands.

1751
03:05:32,830 --> 03:05:36,038
Then we gather our full strength
and march on the Black Gate.

1752
03:05:36,125 --> 03:05:37,490
[COUGHS]

1753
03:05:37,585 --> 03:05:39,917
We cannot achieve victory
through strength of arms.

1754
03:05:40,004 --> 03:05:41,414
ARAGORN:
Not for ourselves.

1755
03:05:41,505 --> 03:05:47,171
But we can give Frodo his chance
if we keep Sauron's Eye fixed upon us.

1756
03:05:48,971 --> 03:05:52,759
Keep him blind to all else that moves.

1757
03:05:53,517 --> 03:05:54,723
A diversion.

1758
03:05:54,810 --> 03:05:56,721
Certainty of death...

1759
03:05:56,812 --> 03:05:59,554
...small chance of success...

1760
03:06:00,483 --> 03:06:02,019
...what are we waiting for?

1761
03:06:02,652 --> 03:06:05,018
Sauron will suspect a trap.

1762
03:06:05,863 --> 03:06:07,854
He will not take the bait.

1763
03:06:09,367 --> 03:06:11,858
Oh, I think he will.

1764
03:06:22,004 --> 03:06:24,040
[CRACKLING]

1765
03:06:43,401 --> 03:06:46,188
[SAURON SPEAKING
IN BLACK SPEECH]

1766
03:06:46,278 --> 03:06:48,894
Long have you hunted me.

1767
03:06:49,824 --> 03:06:51,064
Long have I eluded you.

1768
03:06:52,910 --> 03:06:54,525
No more.

1769
03:06:56,247 --> 03:06:58,613
Behold the Sword of Elendil.

1770
03:07:43,127 --> 03:07:45,618
ÉOWYN:
The city has fallen silent.

1771
03:07:47,298 --> 03:07:50,381
There is no warmth left in the sun.

1772
03:07:51,135 --> 03:07:52,875
It grows so cold.

1773
03:07:55,890 --> 03:07:58,927
It's just the damp
of the first spring rain.

1774
03:08:05,316 --> 03:08:08,479
I do not believe this darkness
will endure.

1775
03:08:35,346 --> 03:08:37,052
[HORN BLOWING]

1776
03:08:37,139 --> 03:08:38,675
SAM:
Look, the Orcs...

1777
03:08:39,225 --> 03:08:41,216
...they're moving off.

1778
03:08:42,311 --> 03:08:44,393
You see, Mr. Frodo...

1779
03:08:44,480 --> 03:08:46,892
...some luck at last.

1780
03:08:46,982 --> 03:08:48,847
ORC SERGEANT:
Move it, you slugs!

1781
03:08:50,194 --> 03:08:53,527
Come on! Faster!

1782
03:09:01,539 --> 03:09:04,872
Come along, you scum....

1783
03:09:04,959 --> 03:09:09,202
I'll whip you down to the bone, you....

1784
03:09:12,091 --> 03:09:13,752
Come on!

1785
03:09:13,843 --> 03:09:16,255
What have I told you?!

1786
03:09:16,345 --> 03:09:18,210
[ORC SERGEANT YELLING
INDISTINCTLY]

1787
03:09:23,060 --> 03:09:24,550
Get up!

1788
03:09:24,979 --> 03:09:27,641
Come on, you slugs!

1789
03:09:27,731 --> 03:09:31,440
You two are going straight
to the front line!

1790
03:09:31,527 --> 03:09:36,521
Now, move it! Go on!
Fall in! Move it!

1791
03:09:49,503 --> 03:09:53,291
To the Gate, you slugs!
Now, move it!

1792
03:10:02,725 --> 03:10:06,263
Don't you know we're at war?

1793
03:10:07,313 --> 03:10:09,645
[ORCS GROWLING AND GRUNTING]

1794
03:10:28,626 --> 03:10:31,459
ORC SERGEANT:
Company, halt!

1795
03:10:31,754 --> 03:10:33,790
[HORN BLOWING]

1796
03:10:35,299 --> 03:10:38,712
Inspection!

1797
03:10:38,802 --> 03:10:41,339
FRODO:
Sam, help me.

1798
03:10:41,430 --> 03:10:43,295
SAM:
Mr. Frodo!

1799
03:10:46,060 --> 03:10:48,642
Stand up, Mr. Frodo.
Stand up!

1800
03:10:48,729 --> 03:10:50,594
FRODO:
It's so heavy.

1801
03:10:54,944 --> 03:10:56,684
[GROWLS AND SNORTS]

1802
03:10:59,698 --> 03:11:00,858
SAM:
Oh, no.

1803
03:11:03,827 --> 03:11:05,488
[ROARS]

1804
03:11:06,497 --> 03:11:08,488
What do I do?
What do we do?

1805
03:11:11,377 --> 03:11:12,742
FRODO: Hit me.
SAM: What?

1806
03:11:12,836 --> 03:11:14,997
FRODO:
Hit me, Sam. Start fighting.

1807
03:11:15,089 --> 03:11:16,670
SAM:
Get off of me!

1808
03:11:17,341 --> 03:11:19,673
Nobody pushes me, you filthy maggot.

1809
03:11:28,352 --> 03:11:30,343
Get off of me!

1810
03:11:31,313 --> 03:11:33,178
Break it up! Break it up!

1811
03:11:35,734 --> 03:11:40,398
Oi! I'll have your guts if you don't
shut this rabble down!

1812
03:11:40,489 --> 03:11:42,855
FRODO:
Go, Sam. Now!

1813
03:11:51,750 --> 03:11:53,365
Move along, scum!

1814
03:11:53,460 --> 03:11:55,371
Back in the line!

1815
03:11:55,879 --> 03:11:57,710
You maggots!

1816
03:11:58,382 --> 03:12:01,374
Get back into the line,
you slugs!

1817
03:12:03,762 --> 03:12:07,220
Dig it, you slugs. Move it.

1818
03:12:07,516 --> 03:12:09,552
[THUNDER RUMBLING]

1819
03:12:09,935 --> 03:12:11,891
Move it!

1820
03:12:40,549 --> 03:12:43,086
[THUNDER RUMBLING]

1821
03:12:48,891 --> 03:12:50,427
[GRUNTS]

1822
03:12:53,979 --> 03:12:55,935
[PANTING]

1823
03:12:56,023 --> 03:12:58,139
I can't....

1824
03:12:58,233 --> 03:13:01,976
I can't....
I can't manage the Ring, Sam.

1825
03:13:02,237 --> 03:13:03,352
It's.... It's....

1826
03:13:03,447 --> 03:13:06,109
It's such a weight to carry.

1827
03:13:06,950 --> 03:13:08,065
It....

1828
03:13:08,160 --> 03:13:10,116
Such a weight.

1829
03:13:15,125 --> 03:13:17,582
We're going that way.
Straight as we can.

1830
03:13:19,004 --> 03:13:22,121
There's no point carrying anything
we're not sure to need.

1831
03:13:26,470 --> 03:13:27,926
[CLANGING]

1832
03:13:37,314 --> 03:13:39,145
Mr. Frodo.

1833
03:13:40,651 --> 03:13:42,141
Look.

1834
03:13:44,780 --> 03:13:46,611
There is light...

1835
03:13:46,949 --> 03:13:49,361
...and beauty up there...

1836
03:13:49,451 --> 03:13:51,237
...that no shadow can touch.

1837
03:13:54,998 --> 03:13:56,829
[WHEEZING]

1838
03:14:07,970 --> 03:14:10,006
[THUNDER RUMBLING]

1839
03:14:42,296 --> 03:14:43,877
Take mine.

1840
03:14:44,381 --> 03:14:46,542
There's a few drops left.

1841
03:15:01,732 --> 03:15:04,348
There will be none left
for the return journey.

1842
03:15:05,235 --> 03:15:08,398
I don't think there will be
a return journey, Mr. Frodo.

1843
03:15:54,952 --> 03:15:57,443
[VOICE OF THE RING WHISPERING]

1844
03:16:01,291 --> 03:16:03,452
Frodo, get down!

1845
03:16:05,254 --> 03:16:07,119
Hide!

1846
03:16:16,014 --> 03:16:17,379
[GRUNTS]

1847
03:16:17,474 --> 03:16:19,305
Frodo!

1848
03:16:25,148 --> 03:16:26,604
Where are they?

1849
03:17:02,686 --> 03:17:05,678
Let the Lord of the Black Land come forth!

1850
03:17:06,648 --> 03:17:09,481
Let justice be done upon him!

1851
03:17:20,954 --> 03:17:23,445
[GATE CREAKING]

1852
03:17:52,986 --> 03:17:56,899
My master, Sauron the Great,
bids thee welcome.

1853
03:18:02,746 --> 03:18:06,489
Is there any in this rout
with authority to treat with me?

1854
03:18:06,875 --> 03:18:09,992
We do not come to treat with Sauron...

1855
03:18:10,087 --> 03:18:13,124
...faithless and accursed.

1856
03:18:13,215 --> 03:18:16,753
Tell your master this:
The armies of Mordor must disband.

1857
03:18:16,843 --> 03:18:19,630
He is to depart these lands,
never to return.

1858
03:18:19,721 --> 03:18:23,088
Aha. Old Greybeard.

1859
03:18:24,559 --> 03:18:28,802
I have a token I was bidden
to show thee.

1860
03:18:33,819 --> 03:18:35,150
Frodo.

1861
03:18:38,031 --> 03:18:39,441
Frodo.

1862
03:18:40,450 --> 03:18:41,656
-Silence.
-No!

1863
03:18:42,536 --> 03:18:43,821
Silence!

1864
03:18:45,622 --> 03:18:49,410
The Halfling was dear to thee, I see.

1865
03:18:50,419 --> 03:18:54,503
Know that he suffered greatly
at the hands of his host.

1866
03:18:54,589 --> 03:18:56,170
[GROWLS]

1867
03:18:59,970 --> 03:19:05,761
Who would've thought one so small
could endure so much pain?

1868
03:19:08,353 --> 03:19:10,514
And he did, Gandalf.

1869
03:19:10,605 --> 03:19:12,436
He did.

1870
03:19:14,609 --> 03:19:16,270
[LAUGHS]

1871
03:19:19,448 --> 03:19:20,984
And who is this?

1872
03:19:21,074 --> 03:19:23,190
Isildur's heir?

1873
03:19:23,285 --> 03:19:26,322
It takes more to make a king
than a broken Elvish blade.

1874
03:19:27,164 --> 03:19:29,120
[YELLS]

1875
03:19:31,126 --> 03:19:33,663
I guess that concludes negotiations.

1876
03:19:35,839 --> 03:19:36,999
I do not believe it.

1877
03:19:39,009 --> 03:19:40,294
I will not.

1878
03:19:40,844 --> 03:19:43,586
[GROWLING]

1879
03:19:56,526 --> 03:19:58,312
Pull back.

1880
03:19:58,612 --> 03:20:00,648
Pull back!

1881
03:20:03,366 --> 03:20:05,527
[ORCS CHANTING]

1882
03:20:12,876 --> 03:20:14,867
SAM:
It's gone, Mr. Frodo.

1883
03:20:17,380 --> 03:20:20,417
The light's passed on,
away towards the north.

1884
03:20:20,509 --> 03:20:22,374
Something's drawn its gaze.

1885
03:20:39,903 --> 03:20:42,645
Hold your ground! Hold your ground.

1886
03:20:44,741 --> 03:20:48,734
Sons of Gondor, of Rohan, my brothers!

1887
03:20:51,581 --> 03:20:53,446
I see in your eyes...

1888
03:20:53,875 --> 03:20:57,914
...the same fear that would take
the heart of me.

1889
03:20:59,881 --> 03:21:03,794
A day may come
when the courage of Men fails...

1890
03:21:03,885 --> 03:21:07,298
...when we forsake our friends
and break all bonds of fellowship.

1891
03:21:07,389 --> 03:21:10,096
But it is not this day.

1892
03:21:10,392 --> 03:21:13,475
An hour of wolves
and shattered shields...

1893
03:21:13,562 --> 03:21:16,474
...when the age of Men
comes crashing down.

1894
03:21:16,565 --> 03:21:19,147
But it is not this day.

1895
03:21:19,234 --> 03:21:20,940
This day we fight!

1896
03:21:23,405 --> 03:21:27,114
By all that you hold dear
on this good earth...

1897
03:21:27,200 --> 03:21:31,443
...I bid you stand, Men of the West!

1898
03:21:40,297 --> 03:21:42,128
[STEAM HISSING]

1899
03:22:11,620 --> 03:22:13,281
[GRUNTS]

1900
03:22:59,918 --> 03:23:03,502
Never thought I'd die fighting
side by side with an Elf.

1901
03:23:03,922 --> 03:23:06,288
What about side by side with a friend?

1902
03:23:09,844 --> 03:23:11,550
Aye.

1903
03:23:12,389 --> 03:23:14,175
I could do that.

1904
03:23:44,546 --> 03:23:46,582
Do you remember the Shire,
Mr. Frodo?

1905
03:23:49,592 --> 03:23:51,833
It'll be spring soon.

1906
03:23:52,595 --> 03:23:55,337
And the orchards will be in blossom.

1907
03:23:55,432 --> 03:23:59,141
And the birds will be nesting
in the hazel thicket.

1908
03:24:00,562 --> 03:24:04,555
And they'll be sowing
the summer barley in the lower fields...

1909
03:24:05,608 --> 03:24:09,942
...and eating the first
of the strawberries with cream.

1910
03:24:11,906 --> 03:24:14,397
Do you remember
the taste of strawberries?

1911
03:24:15,952 --> 03:24:17,738
[HOARSELY]
No, Sam.

1912
03:24:17,829 --> 03:24:20,787
I can't recall the taste of food...

1913
03:24:21,958 --> 03:24:25,291
...nor the sound of water...

1914
03:24:25,378 --> 03:24:28,962
...nor the touch of grass.

1915
03:24:29,966 --> 03:24:31,456
I'm...

1916
03:24:32,385 --> 03:24:33,750
...naked in the dark.

1917
03:24:35,430 --> 03:24:37,762
There's-- There's nothing.

1918
03:24:37,849 --> 03:24:42,593
No veil between me
and the wheel of fire.

1919
03:24:43,813 --> 03:24:45,769
I can see him...

1920
03:24:46,149 --> 03:24:47,810
...with my waking eyes.

1921
03:24:48,902 --> 03:24:51,314
Then let us be rid of it...

1922
03:24:51,946 --> 03:24:54,153
...once and for all.

1923
03:24:54,908 --> 03:24:57,024
Come on, Mr. Frodo.

1924
03:24:57,118 --> 03:24:59,780
I can't carry it for you...

1925
03:25:00,163 --> 03:25:02,199
...but I can carry you.

1926
03:25:02,791 --> 03:25:04,497
Come on!

1927
03:25:27,357 --> 03:25:29,814
[SAURON GROWLING]

1928
03:25:34,948 --> 03:25:37,860
SAURON:
<i>Aragorn.</i>

1929
03:25:44,165 --> 03:25:46,201
[SAURON WHISPERING
INDISTINCTLY]

1930
03:25:49,462 --> 03:25:52,044
<i>Elessar.</i>

1931
03:26:04,060 --> 03:26:06,472
For Frodo.

1932
03:26:10,233 --> 03:26:12,895
[YELLING]

1933
03:26:13,486 --> 03:26:15,397
[YELLING]

1934
03:26:41,431 --> 03:26:42,921
Look, Mr. Frodo.

1935
03:26:43,600 --> 03:26:45,807
A doorway.

1936
03:26:46,436 --> 03:26:48,097
We're almost there.

1937
03:26:50,440 --> 03:26:54,399
Clever Hobbits to climb so high!

1938
03:26:57,322 --> 03:26:59,438
[SCREAMS, GRUNTS]

1939
03:27:08,291 --> 03:27:09,952
Mustn't go that way.

1940
03:27:11,544 --> 03:27:14,001
Mustn't hurt the precious.

1941
03:27:14,088 --> 03:27:15,953
You swore!

1942
03:27:16,049 --> 03:27:18,131
You swore on the precious!

1943
03:27:20,053 --> 03:27:21,964
Sméagol promised!

1944
03:27:22,931 --> 03:27:24,922
Sméagol lied.

1945
03:27:32,815 --> 03:27:34,305
[YELLS]

1946
03:27:34,400 --> 03:27:36,482
[COUGHS]

1947
03:27:58,800 --> 03:28:00,256
[FELL BEASTS ROARING]

1948
03:28:00,343 --> 03:28:01,833
[RINGWRAITHS SCREECHING]

1949
03:28:07,141 --> 03:28:08,972
[SCREAMS]

1950
03:28:14,190 --> 03:28:15,851
[SCREAMS]

1951
03:28:17,402 --> 03:28:19,313
Frodo!

1952
03:28:32,375 --> 03:28:34,661
[RINGWRAITH SCREECHING]

1953
03:28:46,389 --> 03:28:48,175
Eagles.

1954
03:28:49,559 --> 03:28:51,049
The eagles are coming!

1955
03:29:13,916 --> 03:29:15,747
Frodo!

1956
03:29:21,049 --> 03:29:22,289
I'm here, Sam.

1957
03:29:29,766 --> 03:29:31,427
Destroy it!

1958
03:29:41,944 --> 03:29:45,311
Go on! Now!

1959
03:29:45,406 --> 03:29:47,988
Throw it in the fire!

1960
03:29:48,076 --> 03:29:50,442
[PANTING]

1961
03:30:01,339 --> 03:30:04,001
What are you waiting for?

1962
03:30:05,927 --> 03:30:08,293
Just let it go!

1963
03:30:22,235 --> 03:30:24,726
[VOICE OF THE RING WHISPERING]

1964
03:30:41,504 --> 03:30:43,745
The Ring is mine.

1965
03:30:47,301 --> 03:30:49,007
No.

1966
03:30:49,470 --> 03:30:50,755
No.

1967
03:30:59,188 --> 03:31:01,850
No!

1968
03:31:02,900 --> 03:31:05,016
[RINGWRAITHS SCREECHING]

1969
03:31:29,594 --> 03:31:31,505
[FRODO YELLING]

1970
03:31:38,227 --> 03:31:39,888
[ROARING]

1971
03:31:47,195 --> 03:31:49,231
[FRODO AND GOLLUM GRUNTING]

1972
03:31:58,706 --> 03:32:00,412
[AGONIZED SCREAM]

1973
03:32:10,092 --> 03:32:11,923
[GROANING]

1974
03:32:38,371 --> 03:32:40,453
[VOICE MUTED]

1975
03:32:44,627 --> 03:32:46,163
[GOLLUM CACKLING]

1976
03:32:46,254 --> 03:32:48,119
GOLLUM:
Yes!

1977
03:32:49,298 --> 03:32:51,004
Yes!

1978
03:32:52,134 --> 03:32:55,046
Precious! Precious!

1979
03:32:55,137 --> 03:32:58,049
Precious! Precious!

1980
03:32:58,140 --> 03:32:59,880
[LAUGHING]

1981
03:33:07,984 --> 03:33:09,394
[ROARS]

1982
03:33:51,319 --> 03:33:53,150
Give me your hand!

1983
03:34:01,495 --> 03:34:03,861
Take my hand!

1984
03:34:06,542 --> 03:34:07,873
No!

1985
03:34:15,176 --> 03:34:17,087
Don't you let go.

1986
03:34:21,724 --> 03:34:23,260
Don't let go.

1987
03:34:24,894 --> 03:34:26,384
Reach!

1988
03:34:39,116 --> 03:34:42,233
[SCREECHING]

1989
03:35:07,019 --> 03:35:09,510
[SCREECHING,
DEEP RUMBLING]

1990
03:35:11,273 --> 03:35:13,559
[CRACKING]

1991
03:35:55,568 --> 03:35:58,435
Frodo!

1992
03:35:58,988 --> 03:36:01,980
Frodo!

1993
03:36:48,412 --> 03:36:50,528
[VOICE MUTED]

1994
03:37:17,900 --> 03:37:19,731
[EXHALES SOFTLY]

1995
03:37:23,405 --> 03:37:25,236
It's gone.

1996
03:37:29,703 --> 03:37:31,409
It's done.

1997
03:37:31,914 --> 03:37:33,905
SAM:
Yes, Mr. Frodo.

1998
03:37:35,292 --> 03:37:37,749
It's over now.

1999
03:37:40,047 --> 03:37:42,288
[EXPLOSION]

2000
03:37:53,102 --> 03:37:55,218
[PANTING SOFTLY]

2001
03:38:03,404 --> 03:38:05,770
I can see the Shire.

2002
03:38:07,950 --> 03:38:10,282
The Brandywine River.

2003
03:38:12,454 --> 03:38:14,445
Bag End.

2004
03:38:16,792 --> 03:38:19,454
Gandalf's fireworks.

2005
03:38:19,920 --> 03:38:23,629
The lights in the Party Tree.

2006
03:38:25,134 --> 03:38:28,297
Rosie Cotton dancing.

2007
03:38:29,430 --> 03:38:32,137
She had ribbons in her hair.

2008
03:38:35,019 --> 03:38:37,977
If ever I was to marry someone...

2009
03:38:38,939 --> 03:38:41,146
...it would've been her.

2010
03:38:42,610 --> 03:38:44,646
It would've been her.

2011
03:38:44,987 --> 03:38:47,103
[SAM SOBBING]

2012
03:38:56,832 --> 03:38:59,995
I'm glad to be with you,
Samwise Gamgee...

2013
03:39:04,340 --> 03:39:07,252
...here at the end of all things.

2014
03:39:43,921 --> 03:39:46,037
[EAGLES SCREECHING]

2015
03:40:27,589 --> 03:40:30,331
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

2016
03:40:56,952 --> 03:40:58,943
Gandalf?

2017
03:41:04,752 --> 03:41:06,993
[LAUGHING]

2018
03:41:08,756 --> 03:41:10,792
[LAUGHING]

2019
03:41:18,640 --> 03:41:20,631
Frodo!

2020
03:41:40,412 --> 03:41:42,198
Gimli!

2021
03:42:00,557 --> 03:42:02,218
[VOICE MUTED]

2022
03:42:24,039 --> 03:42:26,371
[VOICE MUTED]

2023
03:43:25,225 --> 03:43:28,934
Now come the days of the king.

2024
03:43:33,942 --> 03:43:36,274
May they be blessed.

2025
03:43:42,034 --> 03:43:43,774
[SIGHS]

2026
03:43:48,290 --> 03:43:50,781
[CHEERING]

2027
03:43:56,590 --> 03:43:59,297
This day does not belong to one man...

2028
03:43:59,384 --> 03:44:01,295
...but to all.

2029
03:44:02,971 --> 03:44:05,929
Let us together rebuild this world...

2030
03:44:06,016 --> 03:44:10,305
...that we may share
in the days of peace.

2031
03:44:22,783 --> 03:44:25,274
[ARAGORN SINGING IN ELVISH]

2032
03:45:04,866 --> 03:45:06,322
[SPEAKS IN ELVISH]

2033
03:46:04,092 --> 03:46:06,208
[CROWD APPLAUDS]

2034
03:46:29,826 --> 03:46:31,612
[LAUGHS]

2035
03:46:44,800 --> 03:46:46,836
My friends...

2036
03:46:52,140 --> 03:46:54,802
...you bow to no one.

2037
03:47:39,020 --> 03:47:41,181
FRODO:
<i>And thus it was.</i>

2038
03:47:41,273 --> 03:47:44,936
<i>A Fourth Age of Middle-earth began.</i>

2039
03:47:45,026 --> 03:47:47,688
<i>And the Fellowship of the Ring...</i>

2040
03:47:47,779 --> 03:47:52,364
<i>...though eternally bound</i>
<i>by friendship and love...</i>

2041
03:47:52,450 --> 03:47:54,862
<i>...was ended.</i>

2042
03:47:59,875 --> 03:48:04,744
<i>Thirteen months to the day since Gandalf</i>
<i>sent us on our long journey...</i>

2043
03:48:04,838 --> 03:48:09,047
<i>...we found ourselves</i>
<i>looking upon a familiar sight.</i>

2044
03:48:11,595 --> 03:48:14,337
<i>We were home.</i>

2045
03:48:20,896 --> 03:48:22,727
Hi.

2046
03:48:34,743 --> 03:48:37,234
[HOBBITS CHATTERING
AND LAUGHING]

2047
03:48:39,915 --> 03:48:42,122
Hey, watch the pumpkin.

2048
03:48:49,841 --> 03:48:51,456
Hey!

2049
03:49:30,131 --> 03:49:31,837
MALE PATRON:
More of the same, Rosie.

2050
03:49:31,925 --> 03:49:33,961
Good night, lads.

2051
03:49:52,445 --> 03:49:53,810
[EXHALES]

2052
03:49:55,615 --> 03:49:57,480
[LAUGHING]

2053
03:50:05,417 --> 03:50:07,908
[GUESTS APPLAUDING
AND CHEERING]

2054
03:50:18,513 --> 03:50:19,969
PIPPIN:
Hm?

2055
03:50:31,526 --> 03:50:35,519
FRODO: <i>How do you pick up the threads</i>
<i>of an old life?</i>

2056
03:50:36,865 --> 03:50:39,106
<i>How do you go on...</i>

2057
03:50:39,200 --> 03:50:44,490
<i>...when in your heart</i>
<i>you begin to understand...</i>

2058
03:50:45,707 --> 03:50:48,699
<i>...there is no going back?</i>

2059
03:50:49,377 --> 03:50:53,040
<i>There are some things</i>
<i>that time cannot mend...</i>

2060
03:50:53,548 --> 03:50:56,506
<i>...some hurts that go too deep...</i>

2061
03:50:58,219 --> 03:51:01,052
<i>...that have taken hold.</i>

2062
03:51:33,505 --> 03:51:34,790
[DOOR OPENS]

2063
03:51:39,260 --> 03:51:41,091
SAM:
Mr. Frodo?

2064
03:51:44,432 --> 03:51:45,797
What is it?

2065
03:51:47,644 --> 03:51:51,603
It's been four years to the day
since Weathertop, Sam.

2066
03:51:52,273 --> 03:51:55,015
It's never really healed.

2067
03:51:58,947 --> 03:52:04,237
"<i>There and Back Again: A Hobbit's Tale</i>
by Bilbo Baggins.

2068
03:52:04,953 --> 03:52:08,787
And <i>The Lord of the Rings</i>
by Frodo Baggins."

2069
03:52:09,290 --> 03:52:11,451
You finished it.

2070
03:52:14,295 --> 03:52:15,785
FRODO:
Not quite.

2071
03:52:16,631 --> 03:52:19,122
There's room for a little more.

2072
03:52:21,803 --> 03:52:26,046
FRODO: <i>Bilbo once told me his part</i>
<i>in this tale would end...</i>

2073
03:52:26,141 --> 03:52:29,474
<i>...that each of us must come and go</i>
<i>in the telling.</i>

2074
03:52:30,353 --> 03:52:33,186
<i>Bilbo's story was now over.</i>

2075
03:52:33,690 --> 03:52:36,682
<i>There would be no more journeys</i>
<i>for him...</i>

2076
03:52:36,776 --> 03:52:38,312
<i>...save one.</i>

2077
03:52:39,112 --> 03:52:42,696
BILBO [WEAKLY]:
Tell me again, lad, where are we going?

2078
03:52:42,782 --> 03:52:44,864
FRODO:
To the harbor, Bilbo.

2079
03:52:44,951 --> 03:52:47,738
The Elves have accorded you
a special honor...

2080
03:52:47,829 --> 03:52:50,491
...a place on the last ship
to leave Middle-earth.

2081
03:52:52,208 --> 03:52:53,869
Frodo...

2082
03:52:55,336 --> 03:52:59,830
...any chance of seeing
that old Ring of mine again?

2083
03:53:00,508 --> 03:53:02,715
The one I gave you.

2084
03:53:06,347 --> 03:53:08,508
I'm sorry, Uncle.

2085
03:53:11,102 --> 03:53:13,718
I'm afraid I lost it.

2086
03:53:13,813 --> 03:53:15,678
Oh.

2087
03:53:16,316 --> 03:53:17,726
Pity.

2088
03:53:20,528 --> 03:53:24,362
I should like to have held it
one last time.

2089
03:53:32,874 --> 03:53:34,910
[SEAGULLS CAWING]

2090
03:53:49,349 --> 03:53:51,010
Oh!

2091
03:53:53,561 --> 03:53:58,555
Well, here's a sight
I have never seen before.

2092
03:54:12,747 --> 03:54:16,080
The power of the Three Rings is ended.

2093
03:54:16,918 --> 03:54:19,751
The time has come...

2094
03:54:19,837 --> 03:54:23,170
...for the dominion of Men.

2095
03:54:24,175 --> 03:54:27,087
[IN ELVISH]

2096
03:54:35,562 --> 03:54:37,769
I think I'm...

2097
03:54:37,855 --> 03:54:42,269
...quite ready
for another adventure.

2098
03:55:13,308 --> 03:55:15,674
Farewell...

2099
03:55:15,768 --> 03:55:18,510
...my brave Hobbits.

2100
03:55:20,481 --> 03:55:22,472
My work is now finished.

2101
03:55:26,446 --> 03:55:31,315
Here at last,
on the shores of the sea...

2102
03:55:31,993 --> 03:55:34,826
...comes the end of our Fellowship.

2103
03:55:38,333 --> 03:55:40,824
I will not say, "Do not weep"...

2104
03:55:41,502 --> 03:55:45,495
...for not all tears are an evil.

2105
03:56:03,066 --> 03:56:05,022
It is time, Frodo.

2106
03:56:10,531 --> 03:56:12,522
SAM:
What does he mean?

2107
03:56:15,036 --> 03:56:17,869
We set out to save the Shire, Sam.

2108
03:56:19,499 --> 03:56:22,206
And it has been saved.

2109
03:56:25,880 --> 03:56:28,542
But not for me.

2110
03:56:29,509 --> 03:56:31,921
You don't mean that.

2111
03:56:33,179 --> 03:56:35,215
You can't leave.

2112
03:56:43,731 --> 03:56:46,393
The last pages are for you, Sam.

2113
04:00:19,530 --> 04:00:22,397
FRODO:
<i>My dear Sam:</i>

2114
04:00:24,285 --> 04:00:27,652
<i>You cannot always be torn in two.</i>

2115
04:00:27,747 --> 04:00:31,956
<i>You will have to be one and whole</i>
<i>for many years.</i>

2116
04:00:32,668 --> 04:00:38,129
<i>You have so much to enjoy</i>
<i>and to be and to do.</i>

2117
04:00:39,425 --> 04:00:42,588
<i>Your part in the story will go on.</i>

2118
04:00:43,304 --> 04:00:45,090
Well...

2119
04:00:46,974 --> 04:00:48,635
...I'm back.

2120
04:00:52,313 --> 04:00:54,429
[CHUCKLES]

2121
04:02:29,035 --> 04:02:31,117
[ANNIE LENNOX SINGING
"INTO THE WEST"]

2122
04:02:31,203 --> 04:02:35,242
<i>Lay down</i>

2123
04:02:36,876 --> 04:02:41,245
<i>Your sweet and weary head</i>

2124
04:02:42,965 --> 04:02:46,583
<i>Night is falling</i>

2125
04:02:47,261 --> 04:02:52,096
<i>You have come</i>
<i>To journey's end</i>

2126
04:02:52,767 --> 04:02:56,555
<i>Sleep now</i>

2127
04:02:56,645 --> 04:03:02,311
<i>And dream</i>
<i>Of the ones who came before</i>

2128
04:03:04,111 --> 04:03:08,070
<i>They are calling</i>

2129
04:03:08,157 --> 04:03:12,275
<i>From across</i>
<i>The distant shore</i>

2130
04:03:13,913 --> 04:03:18,828
<i>Why do you weep?</i>

2131
04:03:18,918 --> 04:03:24,003
<i>What are these tears</i>
<i>Upon your face?</i>

2132
04:03:24,090 --> 04:03:29,210
<i>Soon you will see</i>

2133
04:03:29,303 --> 04:03:34,343
<i>All of your fears</i>
<i>Will pass away</i>

2134
04:03:34,433 --> 04:03:39,644
<i>Safe in my arms</i>

2135
04:03:39,730 --> 04:03:44,315
<i>You're only sleeping</i>

2136
04:03:44,401 --> 04:03:49,486
<i>What can you see</i>

2137
04:03:49,573 --> 04:03:54,863
<i>On the horizon?</i>

2138
04:03:54,954 --> 04:03:59,539
<i>Why do the white gulls</i>

2139
04:03:59,625 --> 04:04:04,369
<i>Call?</i>

2140
04:04:05,548 --> 04:04:10,212
<i>Across the sea</i>

2141
04:04:10,302 --> 04:04:15,672
<i>A pale moon rises</i>

2142
04:04:15,766 --> 04:04:18,553
<i>The ships have come</i>

2143
04:04:18,644 --> 04:04:24,480
<i>To carry you home</i>

2144
04:04:26,694 --> 04:04:31,279
<i>And all will turn</i>

2145
04:04:31,365 --> 04:04:36,780
<i>To silver glass</i>

2146
04:04:36,871 --> 04:04:41,240
<i>A light on the water</i>

2147
04:04:41,333 --> 04:04:46,919
<i>All souls pass</i>

2148
04:04:47,006 --> 04:04:51,215
<i>Hope fades</i>

2149
04:04:52,803 --> 04:04:57,718
<i>Into the world of night</i>

2150
04:04:58,392 --> 04:05:02,226
<i>Through shadows falling</i>

2151
04:05:03,063 --> 04:05:08,228
<i>Out of memory and time</i>

2152
04:05:08,903 --> 04:05:12,612
<i>Don't say</i>

2153
04:05:13,407 --> 04:05:18,401
<i>We have come now to the end</i>

2154
04:05:19,246 --> 04:05:23,740
<i>White shores are calling</i>

2155
04:05:23,834 --> 04:05:27,452
<i>You and I will meet again</i>

2156
04:05:27,546 --> 04:05:34,042
<i>And you'll be here</i>
<i>In my arms</i>

2157
04:05:35,262 --> 04:05:39,346
<i>Just sleeping</i>

2158
04:05:39,433 --> 04:05:44,348
<i>What can you see</i>

2159
04:05:44,438 --> 04:05:49,478
<i>On the horizon?</i>

2160
04:05:49,568 --> 04:05:54,483
<i>Why do the white gulls</i>

2161
04:05:54,573 --> 04:06:00,034
<i>Call?</i>

2162
04:06:00,120 --> 04:06:05,331
<i>Across the sea</i>

2163
04:06:05,417 --> 04:06:10,502
<i>A pale moon rises</i>

2164
04:06:10,589 --> 04:06:13,456
<i>The ships have come</i>

2165
04:06:13,550 --> 04:06:19,921
<i>To carry you home</i>

2166
04:06:21,141 --> 04:06:26,261
<i>And all will turn</i>

2167
04:06:26,814 --> 04:06:31,683
<i>To silver glass</i>

2168
04:06:31,777 --> 04:06:36,020
<i>A light on the water</i>

2169
04:06:36,115 --> 04:06:40,028
<i>Grey ships pass</i>

2170
04:06:40,119 --> 04:06:45,830
<i>Into the West</i>
